ATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:11:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/91f562cd474f3708615325e3cf1d373ef1f44857","node_id":"C_kwDOUFB7dNoAKDkxZjU2MmNkNDc0ZjM3MDg2MTUzMjVlM2NmMWQzNzNlZjFmNDQ4NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c","sha":"abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed","sha":"75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed"}],"sha":"91f562cd474f3708615325e3cf1d373ef1f44857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/91f562cd474f3708615325e3cf1d373ef1f44857"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:35:51Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:35:51Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"message":"Make fail-closed consent legible instead of looking broken\n\nReported as \"?habitat= no longer swaps personalizations\". It was not a break: the\nconsent work landed fail-closed, so with no cmp-consent cookie there is no page\nevent, no selections, and every block correctly renders its baseline. But the\ndemo panel was hidden behind an env flag that defaulted off, so there was neither\na way to grant consent nor any indication of why content had gone baseline.\n\nFail-closed stays the default — an absent cookie is not consent, and this is the\nexample most likely to be copied into production. What changes is legibility:\n\n- The demo panel now renders by default. Set\n  CONTENTFUL_OPTIMIZATION_DEMO_CONTROLS=false for a clean render with markup\n  identical to the Next.js original.\n- The panel server-renders WHY personalization is off, distinguishing \"no\n  decision recorded yet\" from \"consent declined\", and points at ?habitat=. It is\n  rendered server-side so there is no flash of the wrong state and it stays\n  correct with JS disabled.\n- The Grant button is highlighted while granting is the useful action, and the\n  consent state is server-rendered rather than populated by JS.\n\nRejected: treating an absent cookie as consent granted. It would have restored\nthe old out-of-the-box behaviour, but baking a permissive default into a consent\nexample is exactly the wrong thing to hand someone.\n\nAlso documents the first-run behaviour in README Getting Started (where it is\nfirst hit), the reasoning in ADR 0004, and the symptom in AGENTS.md under\ngotchas-that-look-like-bugs, since it presents as one.\n\n96 smoke assertions (6 new covering the notice and server-rendered state).","tree":{"sha":"e6ac16ff660cadfd8022924bc4dcbf6b5308e7e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/trees/e6ac16ff660cadfd8022924bc4dcbf6b5308e7e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/commits/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed","node_id":"C_kwDOUFB7dNoAKDc1ZmVmY2E2ZDc0NDYyODhjYjY1ZWYzNWQxY2EwZGRjNzllNDM4ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16","sha":"9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16"}],"sha":"75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/75fefca6d7446288cb65ef35d1ca0ddc79e438ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:10:42Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:10:42Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"message":"README: document how each capability works, with links to the code\n\nMirrors the PR description''s per-capability breakdown into the README so the\nexplanation lives with the code rather than only in a pull request.\n\nEach of Live Preview, variant selection, page tracking, interaction tracking,\ntrack, identify, consent and audience simulation now gets a short paragraph on\nthe mechanism plus links to the modules that implement it — including the\nreasoning a reader would otherwise have to reverse-engineer, such as why\nresolution runs outside JSX, why the browser always skips the page event, why\ndisconnect() is empty, and why allowedEventTypes: [] is required rather than\ndefensive.\n\nThe status table drops its \"Where\" column, which the new sections now carry.\n\nPointers use symbol names rather than line numbers so they do not rot silently as\nthe code moves.","tree":{"sha":"ea1a9612000d32c8279a35d49706fcd30962e371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/trees/ea1a9612000d32c8279a35d49706fcd30962e371"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/commits/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16","node_id":"C_kwDOUFB7dNoAKDliNDMzMzFmZmEyMDY3NDZjYzY2YjkxNGVhOGNhYjQ3NjcxZTFhMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003","sha":"4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003"}],"sha":"9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/9b43331ffa206746cc66b914ea8cab47671e1a16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T02:22:05Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T02:22:05Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"message":"Add Contentful Personalization via the Optimization SDK\n\nImplements server-side variant selection on Hotwire using\n@contentful/optimization-node, browser interaction tracking with\n@contentful/optimization-web, and the first-party preview panel bridged back to\nthe server over a Turbo Stream. Executes docs/optimization-sdk-hotwire-fit.md,\nwhich was an assessment only.\n\nVariants are selected on the server, so personalized content is present in the\ninitial HTML: no client-side swap, no flash of baseline, and only the selected\nvariant is ever sent to the browser.\n\nWhat is included:\n\n- Variant selection in a pure, network-free module (lib/optimization-render.ts)\n  that runs before JSX, so a resolver failure is a clean 500 rather than a\n  truncated body — and is testable without credentials.\n- The page event, which is what returns variant selections, emitted server-side\n  from exactly one place (emitPageEvent). The browser always passes\n  initialPageEvent: \"skip\", because a Turbo Drive visit is itself a server\n  request and would otherwise double-count every navigation.\n- Interaction tracking via data-ctfl-* attributes stamped server-side. The Web\n  SDK re-observes the DOM itself, so Turbo swaps and Turbo Stream morphs need no\n  re-binding and the controller''s disconnect() is deliberately empty.\n- track and identify demos behind CONTENTFUL_OPTIMIZATION_DEMO_CONTROLS.\n- Consent read from a third-party CMP cookie, with allowedEventTypes: [] on both\n  runtimes. That is required, not defensive: the SDK''s admission check falls\n  through to the allow-list whenever consent is not exactly true, and the default\n  list is [''identify'', ''page''] — so consent: false alone still emits a page event\n  and mints a profile.\n- Preview panel audience simulation, bridged to the server through a single\n  writer that always posts both the entry graph and the selections, so a field\n  edit cannot drop a forced audience or vice versa.\n\nNotable constraints, all recorded in ADR 0004:\n\n- Four client bundles, exactly one optimization bundle per page. The panel must\n  share a bundle with the Web SDK (optimization-core''s signals are module-level\n  singletons, so two copies give the panel a different registry) but must never\n  ship to a published visitor.\n- Include depth raised 4 -> 10. The current graph resolves at 4, but that is one\n  level from the edge and unresolved links degrade to baseline silently.\n- Caching stays off; no permutation caching. turbo-cache-control: no-cache now\n  also applies to personalized responses, since Turbo''s page cache would\n  otherwise replay one audience''s HTML for another.\n- Baseline is the structural default at five layers, so an Experience API outage\n  renders baseline rather than the empty region the sibling Next.js demo hit.\n\nAlso: redacts the plaintext revalidation secret in the tracked space export (the\nsecret itself still needs rotating), adds AGENTS.md, and annotates the original\nfit assessment inline where implementation proved it wrong.\n\n90 credential-free smoke assertions; typecheck clean.","tree":{"sha":"ba37917c5f8d15031547be67a219d330bd359559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/trees/ba37917c5f8d15031547be67a219d330bd359559"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/commits/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003","node_id":"C_kwDOUFB7dNoAKDQyMDJlNDI4OWYwYjY0MjEwYmQwMGY5MjZkNDkyMTYzOTQ5NGMwMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commit/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c","sha":"abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c"}],"sha":"4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/4202e4289f0b64210bd00f926d4921639494c003"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-schmidt","id":913312,"login":"eric-schmidt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzMxMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-schmidt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/commits/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:38:31Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T21:38:31Z","email":"e.ryan.schmidt@gmail.com","name":"Eric Schmidt"},"message":"Reimplement demo on Hotwire (Node + TypeScript), replacing Next.js\n\nPorts the Contentful Live Preview demo from Next.js 16 to Hotwire, preserving\nthe markup, class lists, content queries and preview behaviour one-for-one.\n\nThe target is Node + TypeScript, not Rails: Apply Digital confirmed in writing\nthat Allegiant''s Hotwire frontend runs on TypeScript. Hotwire is backend\nagnostic, and staying in JS keeps the `contentful` and `@contentful/live-preview`\npackages working — which is what makes Content Source Maps survive server\nrendering, so Inspector Mode needs no field tagging.\n\nStack: Hono + hono/jsx for server-rendered HTML (no React reaches the browser),\nTurbo Drive for navigation, Stimulus for the remaining JS, Tailwind v4.\n\nThree Next.js primitives had no equivalent and were rebuilt:\n\n- draftMode() -> src/lib/preview.ts, an HMAC cookie keeping the\n  SameSite=None; Secure attributes Contentful''s iframe requires. Resolved once\n  per request by middleware, the equivalent of a Rails before_action.\n- useContentfulLiveUpdates -> a Stimulus controller plus POST /preview/render.\n  The controller posts the SDK''s patched entry graph back; the server re-renders\n  it through the same resolver and replies with a morphing Turbo Stream. Costs\n  zero Contentful requests per keystroke, so the CPA''s 14 req/s limit is never\n  in play.\n- \"use cache\"/cacheTag/revalidateTag -> rebuilt, then removed. See below.\n\nADR 0002''s two-resolver split collapses to one. That split existed only to keep\nLive Preview JS off the published path, which React''s compile-time \"use client\"\nboundary made hard; here the SDK is a separate bundle that only draft renders\nload, so the published path ships none of it structurally.\n\nCaching is deliberately absent. It was implemented as a tag-indexed store\nfaithful to ADR 0001 (tags registered during the fetch so they can reference\nsys.id), but it made the demo worse: a reload after saving in Contentful showed\nnothing until a tag was invalidated. Every request now hits Contentful and\nresponses send Cache-Control: no-store. The implementation is parked verbatim in\nbackup/with-cache/ with restore instructions rather than commented out.\n\nRoutes follow Hotwire convention, not App Router convention. Nothing lives under\n/api, which in a Hotwire app denotes a JSON API; these are controller actions\nreturning HTML. A singular preview resource instead:\n\n    GET    /preview          enter (302)\n    DELETE /preview          leave (303, as Turbo requires after non-GET)\n    POST   /preview/render   re-render as a Turbo Stream\n\nLeaving preview is a form and submit button, not a link: Turbo 8 prefetches\nlinks on hover, so a stateful GET link fires without a click. hono/method-override\nsupplies the _method unwrapping Rack::MethodOverride provides in Rails.\n\nDeliberate deviations from 1:1, with reasoning in the port plan: the alt-text bug\nis fixed (alternativeText lives on the mediaWrapper entry, not the asset''s file\nobject, so every alt was empty); the image chain gets real null guards; / redirects\nto /home instead of serving create-next-app boilerplate; an Exit preview control\nwas added. Duplex''s invisible text-white and the no-op text-md are kept for\nvisual fidelity.\n\nRationale is recorded in docs/plans/2026-08-25-nextjs-to-hotwire-port.md\n(decisions, rejected alternatives, provenance) and ADR 0003.\ndocs/optimization-sdk-hotwire-fit.md assesses how optimization-node/-web would\nattach, for the Allegiant workshop; no personalization code exists yet.\n\nVerified against space zh1nhbmve68h: renders hero + duplex with populated alt\ntext, published path ships no Live Preview JS, preview enter/exit and the Turbo\nStream round trip all behave, and 37 render/escaping assertions pass via\n`npm run smoke`.\n\nNote: contentful-export-zh1nhbmve68h-master-2026-08-11T09-14-44.json still\ncontains a plaintext revalidation secret in a webhook URL and predates this\ncommit. It should be rotated and redacted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4da09a9b0f23a2f0c3fb31d0ba5f710056a5412a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/trees/4da09a9b0f23a2f0c3fb31d0ba5f710056a5412a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eric-schmidt/demo-optimization-sdk-hotwire/git/commits/abe5caaab9902fa574c78202ac8efb60e5e3a65c","verification":{