lder and\nNew Folder, so a layer can be filed without dragging. Both routes share\none move, announced in a live region. Focus follows the row, which\nremounts in its new list, or the folder header when that folder is\nclosed.\n\nRef MAP-41\n\n* fix(web): spell the browser tab title EPIC.map\n\n* fix(widget): report a favourite that cannot be moved yet (MAP-41)\n\nA layer whose own star is still saving has no row id to file, so its\nmenu dims every destination behind a note rather than accepting a click\nit would drop. A folder that fails to save, or refuses the layer after\nsaving, now says so where the layer lands back.\n\nRef MAP-41","tree":{"sha":"171ac194cec98e143fc7502317fbe78768069b8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcgov/EPIC.map/git/trees/171ac194cec98e143fc7502317fbe78768069b8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bcgov/EPIC.map/git/commits/7c11c408b19957736531e4162cd8304f167f68a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 171ac194cec98e143fc7502317fbe78768069b8c\nparent 079ed9724962bedcac1ac0034e1806970348c042\nauthor Shaelyn Tolkamp <46355612+tolkamps1@users.noreply.github.com> 1790181858 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790181858 -0600\n\nMap 41 favourites layer options menu (#20)\n\n* feat(widget): move favourites between groups from a menu (MAP-41)\n\nGive each favourite a kebab menu listing Favourites, every folder and\nNew Folder, so a layer can be filed without dragging. Both routes share\none move, announced in a live region. Focus follows the row, which\nremounts in its new list, or the folder header when that folder is\nclosed.\n\nRef MAP-41\n\n* fix(web): spell the browser tab title EPIC.map\n\n* fix(widget): report a favourite that cannot be moved yet (MAP-41)\n\nA layer whose own star is still saving has no row id to file, so its\nmenu dims every destination behind a note rather than accepting a click\nit would drop. A folder that fails to save, or refuses the layer after\nsaving, now says so where the layer lands back.\n\nRef MAP-41