sers/Bor-Code/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bor-Code/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bor-Code/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bor-Code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bor-Code/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bor-Code","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bor-Code/Global-Climate-Socioeconomic-Impact/commits/815f0dc324f8eb1b13cc3c580615b77e7b3d0d26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:59:10Z","email":"161816964+Bor-Code@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Boran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:59:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: migrate analytical pipeline to unified Jupyter Notebook architecture (#3)\n\n* feat(phase-1): data source schema validation and ERD\n\n- Run API discovery across all 4 sources (WB, OWID, WHR, Berkeley Earth)\n- Confirm World Bank API schema: 8 fields per record, countryiso3code as join key\n- Select OWID CO2 dataset as primary CO2 source (79 cols, WB EN.ATM.CO2E.PC inactive)\n- Confirm Berkeley Earth S3 accessibility for country-level temperature anomaly\n- Determine analysis window: 2005-2022 (18 years, bounded by WHR availability)\n- Define temporal train/test split: 2005-2018 train / 2019-2022 test\n- Document missing data strategy: Gini forward-fill max 3y, CO2 no fill\n- Add dbt sources.yml with real column schemas and freshness thresholds\n- Add docs/phase1_schema_report.md with ERD (Mermaid) and coverage analysis\n- Rewrite README.md in English with academic format\n\n* refactor: translate entire project to English\n\n- Rename analyses/src/faz1_source_discovery.py -> phase1_source_discovery.py\n- Rename docs/faz1_kaynak_dogrulama.json -> docs/phase1_source_validation.json\n- Rewrite all Python files: remove Turkish strings, docstrings, print statements\n- Rewrite all YAML/TOML configs: remove Turkish comments and descriptions\n- Remove all inline comments project-wide (no-comments policy)\n- All test assertion messages now in English\n- Dashboard UI text translated to English\n- .env.example, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Dockerfile, docker-compose fully in English\n- 13/13 pytest passing after translation\n\n* fix: resolve all ruff lint and format violations\n\n- Remove unused sys import from phase1_source_discovery.py\n- Replace EN DASH with ASCII hyphen in dashboard/app.py (RUF001)\n- Remove unused pathlib.Path import from test_constants.py (F401)\n- Fix import sort order in test_constants.py (I001)\n- Auto-format long lines in phase1_source_discovery.py and test_constants.py\n\nAll checks passing: ruff check + ruff format + 13/13 pytest\n\n* fix: translate .gitattributes comments to English to prevent encoding issues\n\n* feat(phase-2): data ingestion script and raw data storage\n\n- Created analyses/src/phase2_ingestion.py to download raw data\n- World Bank API (GDP, Gini, Unemployment, Population) loaded as JSON\n- OWID CO2 dataset downloaded as CSV\n- DuckDB raw schema initialized with ingestion logic\n- WHR placeholder logic added for manual Kaggle CSV ingestion\n\n* Migrate project to Jupyter Notebook architecture with Polars & DuckDB\n\n* Remove obsolete extracted_notebook.py to fix CI","tree":{"sha":"c3e4e96fa0d7b2d7d70b7c41e108f1510d10ad0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bor-Code/Global-Climate-Socioeconomic-Impact/git/trees/c3e4e96fa0d7b2d7d70b7c41e108f1510d10ad0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bor-Code/Global-Climate-Socioeconomic-Impact/git/commits/815f0dc324f8eb1b13cc3c580615b77e7b3d0d26","verification":{"payload":"tree c3e4e96fa0d7b2d7d70b7c41e108f1510d10ad0f\nparent d7b8326b481f196f4a801fdecf6acdde21949c49\nauthor Boran <161816964+Bor-Code@users.noreply.github.com> 1787828350 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787828350 +0300\n\nfeat: migrate analytical pipeline to unified Jupyter Notebook architecture (#3)\n\n* feat(phase-1): data source schema validation and ERD\n\n- Run API discovery across all 4 sources (WB, OWID, WHR, Berkeley Earth)\n- Confirm World Bank API schema: 8 fields per record, countryiso3code as join key\n- Select OWID CO2 dataset as primary CO2 source (79 cols, WB EN.ATM.CO2E.PC inactive)\n- Confirm Berkeley Earth S3 accessibility for country-level temperature anomaly\n- Determine analysis window: 2005-2022 (18 years, bounded by WHR availability)\n- Define temporal train/test split: 2005-2018 train / 2019-2022 test\n- Document missing data strategy: Gini forward-fill max 3y, CO2 no fill\n- Add dbt sources.yml with real column schemas and freshness thresholds\n- Add docs/phase1_schema_report.md with ERD (Mermaid) and coverage analysis\n- Rewrite README.md in English with academic format\n\n* refactor: translate entire project to English\n\n- Rename analyses/src/faz1_source_discovery.py -> phase1_source_discovery.py\n- Rename docs/faz1_kaynak_dogrulama.json -> docs/phase1_source_validation.json\n- Rewrite all Python files: remove Turkish strings, docstrings, print statements\n- Rewrite all YAML/TOML configs: remove Turkish comments and descriptions\n- Remove all inline comments project-wide (no-comments policy)\n- All test assertion messages now in English\n- Dashboard UI text translated to English\n- .env.example, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Dockerfile, docker-compose fully in English\n- 13/13 pytest passing after translation\n\n* fix: resolve all ruff lint and format violations\n\n- Remove unused sys import from phase1_source_discovery.py\n- Replace EN DASH with ASCII hyphen in dashboard/app.py (RUF001)\n- Remove unused pathlib.Path import from test_constants.py (F401)\n- Fix import sort order in test_constants.py (I001)\n- Auto-format long lines in phase1_source_discovery.py and test_constants.py\n\nAll checks passing: ruff check + ruff format + 13/13 pytest\n\n* fix: translate .gitattributes comments to English to prevent encoding issues\n