":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/7fa12f581a677e69c84f66c4cfba2de7a9f50ced/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T06:02:15Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T06:02:15Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: a 10-minute probe for the e2e playwright path\n\nThe baseline reaches cove2e 2h45m in and shows only the TAIL of a failing\nsuite, which for a node crash is the stack rather than the line that names the\nmissing module. This runs the same install and the same invocation and prints\nall of it.","tree":{"sha":"a90fd3a3db1896544236724e302bbac46cf697df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/a90fd3a3db1896544236724e302bbac46cf697df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/7fa12f581a677e69c84f66c4cfba2de7a9f50ced","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/7fa12f581a677e69c84f66c4cfba2de7a9f50ced","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDdmYTEyZjU4MWE2NzdlNjljODRmNjZjNGNmYmEyZGU3YTlmNTBjZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a","sha":"f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a"}],"sha":"7fa12f581a677e69c84f66c4cfba2de7a9f50ced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/7fa12f581a677e69c84f66c4cfba2de7a9f50ced"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:16:49Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:16:49Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"deploy: the compose path serves the MASTER server image, not a release\n\nMeasured 2026-08-22: master client4 calls GET /api/v4/license/client with no\nformat=old and a release server answers 400, which kills the e2e suite in\nglobalSetup before a browser opens - so cove2e captures nothing. The compose\nfile default is a release tag, right for a person running the stack by hand and\nwrong for the suite.","tree":{"sha":"a5657155d0e8e41ab7d3ff5767582bd09ce9850a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/a5657155d0e8e41ab7d3ff5767582bd09ce9850a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGYxZDc2MWU5Y2YwMmZmNmY2MDg5YzQ3OTJmMDUzMGIwYjg3ZDFhNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69","sha":"cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69"}],"sha":"f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f1d761e9cf02ff6f6089c4792f0530b0b87d1a4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:15:45Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:15:45Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"deploy: run the services on docker compose too, not only Apple Container\n\nchainstrip e2e.servicesUp is ONE command and it runs wherever the baseline\nruns. This script probed nothing and called the Apple Container CLI directly,\nso on the Linux CI runner it died with a command-not-found before postgres\nstarted - cove2e brought nothing up, the e2e suite never ran, and covtrim lost\nevery function only a browser executes.\n\ncompose.services.yml already did the whole job for a docker host, CS_COVE2E_WS\nmount included, so this delegates to it rather than reimplementing. The backend\nis chosen by probing for the container CLI, never by a platform name.","tree":{"sha":"757ffb275c787eebd18f51e9ee1ec348ac937e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/757ffb275c787eebd18f51e9ee1ec348ac937e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGNiMDkxNWY3MzlmY2I0MDA2NjRjYjUzZmU4YTkzNDIwNDVjNTVjNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f","sha":"f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f"}],"sha":"cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/cb0915f739fcb400664cb53fe8a9342045c55c69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:13:37Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:13:37Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: install the e2e-tests/playwright project before the baseline\n\ncove2e runs the target''s own e2e suite, and that project is a separate npm\npackage webapp-setup never touches. Without it the suite dies before its first\nspec with a command-not-found, and an e2e suite that never RAN captures nothing\n- so covtrim loses every function only a browser executes, which is what made\nthe 2026-09-03 and 2026-09-04 baselines accept 0 deps.\n\nBrowsers install explicitly rather than through the project''s postinstall,\nwhich fetches chromium AND firefox; test:smoke runs --project=chrome.","tree":{"sha":"f0afe36585e3509c9726b264c8ae68a9a5f934bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/f0afe36585e3509c9726b264c8ae68a9a5f934bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGYwNjM3NzU4MjkwNzM0ZjUyYjFlZDI5OGU2Zjg5N2EyNTAxYTdmMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d","sha":"f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d"}],"sha":"f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f0637758290734f52b1ed298e6f897a2501a7f0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T02:37:55Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T02:37:55Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"config: restore the e2e block, which is where the ESM half of a dual package is executed\n\ncovtrim has accepted 0 deps in every CI baseline of this target, against 2 in an\nattended local run. The cause is not a chainstrip regression - it is missing\nevidence, and the forensics are exact.\n\nThree files disappeared from covtrim''s view between the two runs:\n`@tiptap/core/dist/index.js`, `@tiptap/core/jsx-dev-runtime/index.js` and\n`tinycolor2/esm/tinycolor.js`. All three are the ESM halves of dual-build\npackages, and all three exist in exactly ONE place: the attended run''s\n`cove2e-capture.json`. They are absent from covtoolchain (a build PARSES the ESM\nbranch, it does not EXECUTE it), absent from witness, and absent from the jest\nsuite - which `require`s the CJS half by definition. Only a browser runs the ESM\nhalf.\n\nLosing them halves `functionsTotal` on a byte-identical extraction (@tiptap/core\n1887 -> 1015, tinycolor2 181 -> 93), so every candidate lands at-risk rather than\nproven-dead, and at-risk is held by default. Hence 0 accepted.\n\nThe block is recovered verbatim from 5fb2ffa160, the onboarding commit whose run\nproduced that capture - not reinvented. `webapp/deploy/services.sh`,\n`compose.services.yml` and the playwright workspace are all still present. Note\n`browserCoverage: true` with an explicit `/static/ -> channels/dist` asset map:\nthe covbrowser URL filter defaults to Next''s `/_next/`, so a non-Next target\nrecords nothing without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a8004fcd9ea92d7f3bb22b5987b23971bd97d3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/6a8004fcd9ea92d7f3bb22b5987b23971bd97d3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGY1ZGQ5Yjc5ZDcxNWFhYTkyYjcwMDkwODk3MTlmNDBiNjIwZDUyM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf","sha":"92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf"}],"sha":"f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/f5dd9b79d715aaa92b7009089719f40b620d523d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T00:47:21Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T00:47:21Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"baseline: dispatch only, so a workflow edit stops costing an hour of a runner\n\nA baseline is a MEASUREMENT that occupies a runner for an hour or more, and\nnothing about a push says a measurement is wanted now.\n\nThe `paths-ignore` lists this replaces were a partial fix for the same problem -\nthey grew after a probe push started a full baseline 6 seconds before the probe\nwas dispatched, leaving the measurement queued behind it - but they could not\ncover the case that kept recurring: editing THIS file. Every workflow fix today\n(the artifact upload, the corepack ordering, the node bootstrap) started an\nunwanted baseline, and twice put two runs of the same target in flight at once.\n\nThe old argument for keeping the push trigger was that a change to this file\nDOES change the run. That is true, and it does not follow that the run should\nstart by itself: the person editing it is the person who knows whether a fresh\nmeasurement is worth an hour of the box.\n\n`workflow_dispatch` is unchanged, so every target is still runnable on demand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"372e783fac8cf5d994905a4da28d15b5be81ebdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/372e783fac8cf5d994905a4da28d15b5be81ebdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDkyZWQxZWVjOTk4MDYwZWQ4YTJhNmZhOTNmN2Q5N2IwYjE3NWFkYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e","sha":"97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e"}],"sha":"92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/92ed1eec998060ed8a2a6fa93f7d97b0b175adaf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:06:43Z","email":"kika@agily.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:06:43Z","email":"kika@agily.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"chainstrip: a path to csbox, because package access is per PACKAGE\n\nMEASURED on the first contained CI run, which failed at setup in 60 seconds:\n\n  npm error 403 Forbidden - GET .../@chainstrip%2fcsbox-linux-x64\n  Permission permission_denied: read_package\n\nThis repo''s ambient GITHUB_TOKEN reads @chainstrip/cli and is refused\n@chainstrip/csbox-linux-x64, published minutes earlier from a sibling repo.\nGitHub Packages grants Actions access per package, so a new package starts\nreadable by its own source repo and nothing else — and \"the token already reads\none @chainstrip package\" is no evidence at all about the next one.\n\n`csbox_path` uses an already-installed binary through CHAINSTRIP_CSBOX, the\nresolver''s one explicit override. It is the WEAKER option and the comment says\nso: it ties the run to one machine, which is tolerable only because this runner\nIS one machine. The npm path stays the default and starts working the moment\nthe package is granted Actions read access to this repo — clearing the variable\nis the whole switch back.\n\nThe launcher check is now common to both branches. Only the INSTALL differed,\nand duplicating `--version` and `probe` into each arm would have let one of them\ndrift into not checking.","tree":{"sha":"2a6ae1eaf3704ed2b55abfd0f13dfa22699ca481","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/2a6ae1eaf3704ed2b55abfd0f13dfa22699ca481"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDk3Zjg3ZDkyMTkyOWU0MzBlZmYzZDliOGNmYmY4ODI1MDFkMjBlMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f","sha":"91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f"}],"sha":"97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/97f87d921929e430eff3d9b8cfbf882501d20e0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:03:01Z","email":"kika@agily.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:03:01Z","email":"kika@agily.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"chainstrip: run the baseline CONTAINED\n\nThe pipeline executes customer-controlled dependency code as its core loop, and\nmore of it than this repo''s own CI does — every extracted package''s subpaths\nloaded in both module formats, 88 per-dep suite runs, production builds and a\ncoverage build. Until now every one of those children got the runner''s full\nenvironment, including its HOME and everything reachable from it.\n\n  \"sandbox\": { \"mode\": \"enforce\", \"allowDegraded\": true }\n\n`allowDegraded` is required on THIS runner and is not decoration: `csbox probe`\nrules every phase `partial` because the cgroup is neither delegated nor\ncreatable at the hierarchy root, so the memory ceiling cannot be applied and\npids and file size fall back to rlimits. Without the flag, enforce refuses to\nrun rather than silently degrading.\n\nThe launcher is installed BESIDE the CLI, in the same prefix, because that is\nwhat chainstrip''s own resolution expects: it locates csbox with\n`createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(\"<pkg>/bin/csbox\")` anchored at its own\ndist/cli.mjs, deliberately, because two earlier designs walked the filesystem\nand were defeated by planting a binary. A failed install is fatal — the\nalternative is a run that reports `kernel: false` and completes, which is\nenforcement nobody notices was absent.\n\n`csbox probe` runs and prints before anything else, because \"linux-x64\" is not\nevidence that the kernel can enforce: Landlock can be absent below 5.13 or\nmissing from the boot LSM list, and a run whose phases are `partial` should say\nso in its log rather than in a report nobody opens.\n\nMEASURED before this landed, by hand on this same runner: 88 deps, ZERO\ndivergence from the three uncontained baselines — the same 78 validated, the\nsame ten non-validated deps by name, the same 11,780 -> 859 files and\n49,993,441 -> 20,468,783 bytes, the same buildgate offenders and covtrim and\nfullgate numbers. 1,816 contained children, 3h36m against 3h24-35m uncontained.","tree":{"sha":"ca06aae60f1d6b736c1b6a76157b2f97cf70d2a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/ca06aae60f1d6b736c1b6a76157b2f97cf70d2a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDkxYmUzY2VhNzIwNDZjNjhlMDZiMTE0MzRhN2U0YzUzZmYxM2Q5NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75","sha":"64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75"}],"sha":"91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/91be3cea72046c68e06b11434a7e4c53ff13d94f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:48:29Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:48:29Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: probe the SWEEP path, which is the one that disagrees\n\nvalidate was the wrong instrument. It clones a FRESH workspace per dep and\npasses NO timeout. sweep reuses ONE workspace across every dep and caps each\nisolation run at max(60s, suite x 1.5), about 73s on this runner. A killed run\nreported completed:false, and the old code read that as ''fails in isolation'' —\nwhich is how a file that passes alone 20/20 became a confirmed regression.\n\nBoth differences are ours. So the probe now runs the sweep path itself, limited\nto tier B (21 deps, includes react-overlays) instead of all 88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P5dTKoFgMKj4X8XeCApJg7","tree":{"sha":"141b9f0e373f0fa5dbe6dc099b0110a54104ab09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/141b9f0e373f0fa5dbe6dc099b0110a54104ab09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDY0ZjcxYTFmMjZlMDFmODYzODlkNWNiYTU1MTczOTdlODFiZGZjNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72","sha":"01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72"}],"sha":"64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/64f71a1f26e01f86389d5cba5517397e81bdfc75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:24:16Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:24:16Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: measure the single-file failure RATE, and read the verdict not the exit code\n\nThe last probe counted exit codes. chainstrip validate exits 0 for a\nbaseline-failed verdict too, so its ''clean 3/3'' came from runs whose overlay arm\nnever ran. This parses the verdict line instead.\n\nThe question is now a number, not a yes/no: how often does this one file fail\nalone with the overlay? Two failures in a row are ordinary at a 20% rate and\nstrange at 0%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P5dTKoFgMKj4X8XeCApJg7","tree":{"sha":"61a3404120475dcc47a3d66a2bf6e5658a9602a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/61a3404120475dcc47a3d66a2bf6e5658a9602a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKDAxODY0ZGI2MTk3YjUxMzljNDU3YjQzM2U0ZmQ0MGFmOTk5NThkNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d","sha":"c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d"}],"sha":"01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/01864db6197b5139c457b433e4fd40af99958d72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:45:03Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:45:03Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: probe the FULL mapped set — the single-file version asked the wrong question\n\nThe first probe ran one test file and got 0/5, which settled nothing. The\nbaseline''s overlay arm failed on 48 files, all modal components (react-overlays''\nown surface), so the failure is broad and a single-file run cannot exhibit it —\nand the jsdom leak it is entangled with is CROSS-FILE, so a lone file is exactly\nthe context where it cannot occur.\n\nThis runs the full 609-file mapped set, which is what the sweep validated, so a\nclean result means something and a 48-file failure points at either a real\noverlay regression or cross-dep contamination in the sweep workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P5dTKoFgMKj4X8XeCApJg7","tree":{"sha":"bb6010fa88ec9f768e635dffdf1083bb32a0c468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/bb6010fa88ec9f768e635dffdf1083bb32a0c468"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGM4ODU4YjJiZmQzYjdlNzQ3ODBjOTBmZGJiZjY3MjE0MmUwN2U1N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886","sha":"be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886"}],"sha":"c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/c8858b2bfd3b7e74780c90fdbbf672142e07e57d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:36:11Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:36:11Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: don''t start a 3.7h baseline for a push that cannot change the result\n\nPushing a one-off probe workflow started a full baseline 6s before the probe\nwas dispatched, and on a single self-hosted runner the 15-minute measurement\nsat queued behind it until the baseline was cancelled by hand.\n\npaths-ignore covers what cannot affect what the pipeline measures: probe\nworkflows, the gate workflow, .github/scripts, and Markdown.\nchainstrip-baseline.yml is deliberately NOT ignored — a change to it DOES\nchange the run, which is why this very push triggers one last baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P5dTKoFgMKj4X8XeCApJg7","tree":{"sha":"a89c204e7bcbf216e51bc2e9204d502eb0975653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/a89c204e7bcbf216e51bc2e9204d502eb0975653"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGJlN2IyYjFkODVkMzBlODdlMTcyN2ZjZTg4Njc0OWZkNDI2NTU4ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81","sha":"cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81"}],"sha":"be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/be7b2b1d85d30e87e1727fce886749fd42655886"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/commits/cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T09:37:03Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T09:37:03Z","email":"kika@kikap.com","name":"Kirill Pertsev"},"message":"ci: one-off probe — does react-overlays reproduce on Linux?\n\nOn cli 0.3.8 the same commit validates react-overlays on macOS and rules it\noverlay-failed on the Linux runner. That is not the tool disagreeing with\nitself on the same evidence: Linux CONFIRMED the failure by the isolation\nstandard (delete_post_modal.test.tsx failed alone with the overlay and passed\nalone at stock, twice each), while three hand-run isolation attempts on macOS\ncould not reproduce it at all.\n\nThe open question is exactly one thing — on Linux, does it REPRODUCE? A real\nplatform-specific extraction regression fails every time; an intermittent that\nisolation caught once does not. One observation cannot separate those, so this\nrepeats the same per-file differential N times and reports the ratio.\n\nworkflow_dispatch only, reports and never gates, and runs the single implicated\nfile so each repeat costs seconds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P5dTKoFgMKj4X8XeCApJg7","tree":{"sha":"0c3dd1d86c466992f0f904ce1e884dcdfe7263fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/trees/0c3dd1d86c466992f0f904ce1e884dcdfe7263fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chainstrip/mattermost/git/commits/cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207889?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kika","id":207889,"login":"kika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kika","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/cf890b63a11549c38bc2310e19a89462d4a44c81","node_id":"C_kwDOUFRWYNoAKGNmODkwYjYzYTExNTQ5YzM4YmMyMzEwZTE5YTg5NDYyZDRhNDRjODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chainstrip/mattermost/commit/91f5ceb23c7804bead22e5925aede6f299d0e7d4","sha":"91f5ceb23c7804bead22e5925aede6f299d0e7d4","url