:"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e4779","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/monotykamary/heddlework/commits/87b0fd671ec8135f13fba8d708e099de969578a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:33:15Z","email":"e@4779.ru","name":"Nick Ermakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:33:15Z","email":"e@4779.ru","name":"Nick Ermakov"},"message":"feat(web): switch workspaces and identify hosts over the wire\n\nAdd the switchWorkspace workbench command (union, type list, validator,\nhost-side executor) so the browser can ask the host to open another\ndirectory; the host validates the target as an existing directory before\ncalling the controller. Un-stub RemoteWorkbenchController.switchWorkspace\nto send it.\n\nWelcome frames now carry the host identity (id/name/os/arch/machine/\nversion/protocol persisted next to the host token) and the live workspace\npath instead of the startup-frozen one, and the web client tracks\nalternate host URLs with failure-driven candidate rotation - groundwork\nfor the browser host switcher. CSP relaxes connect-src to ws:/wss: so the\npage may open sockets to other hosts; auth still rides the auth.<token>\nsubprotocol.\n\nPorted from the 0xCUB3 fork''s host-switcher work (post-d55e9adb), adapted\nto upstream''s single-runtime architecture. Refs #22, #27.","tree":{"sha":"a02587e30ffb866327540d3328d03cbc9ce4d70e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/monotykamary/heddlework/git/trees/a02587e30ffb866327540d3328d03cbc9ce4d70e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/monotykamary/heddlework/git/commits/87b0fd671ec8135f13fba8d708e099de969578a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5234703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e4779/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e4779/followers","following_url":"https://api.g