epos/barayuda/sentra/commits/804831076eb9c47bf06d3737d55b2397ca0fcdc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:21:21Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:21:21Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs: correct shell''s recorded entry measurement to 5181B\n\nShell''s index chunk embeds a sha384- integrity digest per remote, so its\ngzipped size depends on the other apps'' built bytes. The recorded 5178B\ncame from a build whose remotes were built with VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS=true.\n5181B is the plain-build figure. Records the mechanism so the next\nre-measurement does not read the drift as a shell regression.","tree":{"sha":"ee3a5db5f4cea89f60a3df241867ea3a56296c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/ee3a5db5f4cea89f60a3df241867ea3a56296c28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/804831076eb9c47bf06d3737d55b2397ca0fcdc2","verification":{"payload":"tree ee3a5db5f4cea89f60a3df241867ea3a56296c28\nparent 7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788218481 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788218481 +0700\n\ndocs: correct shell''s recorded entry measurement to 5181B\n\nShell''s index chunk embeds a sha384- integrity digest per remote, so its\ngzipped size depends on the other apps'' built bytes. The recorded 5178B\ncame from a build whose remotes were built with VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS=true.\n5181B is the plain-build figure. Records the mechanism so the next\nre-measurement does not read the drift as a shell regression.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapYMcRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmJGhAD9HQHMsxr8kUSu14s3le37\nsKzZDKdNw8AQw+CyixywElEA/2Fnxf5z+MeePHaRm3YA0qJsRbFSIGooB8w8DrIu\nZlsB\n=sldy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/804831076eb9c47bf06d3737d55b2397ca0fcdc2","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDgwNDgzMTA3NmViOWM0N2JmMDZkMzczN2Q1NWIyMzk3Y2EwZmNkYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d","sha":"7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d"}],"sha":"804831076eb9c47bf06d3737d55b2397ca0fcdc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/804831076eb9c47bf06d3737d55b2397ca0fcdc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:13:04Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:13:04Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(gates): withdraw M6''s console bundle budget raise, restoring 5632\n\nRe-measured at e9c72dc, apps/console''s entry chunk is 4930B gzipped --\nunder the original 5632B budget, which is also the number the recorded\nrule regenerates from the new measurement (ceil(4930/1024)*1024 = 5120,\n*1.1 = 5632). M6 therefore ships no budget raise at all.\n\nNothing was optimised for size. The entry shrank as a side effect of the\nfinal review''s Critical fix: installing @sentra/flags in console''s\nfederated entry gave the flags runtime a second importer alongside\nmain.ts, so Rollup hoisted it out of the entry into the shared\nfederated-*.js chunk, which has no glob budget and is covered by\n$total:js.\n\nVerified in the built output rather than inferred from the byte drop --\na 968B fall is equally consistent with ''the runtime moved'' and with\n''something was dropped''. ''orders.bulkActions'' and fnv1a''s offset basis\n2166136261 appear in federated-*.js and in neither case in index-*.js;\nui.dataTable.sortBy appears in index-*.js and not in federated-*.js. So\nthe catalogue never moved and the locale analysis still holds -- it is\nsimply no longer load-bearing, because the 266B overage it explained is\ngone.\n\nFalsified the restored budget rather than trusting a green run:\ntemporarily set to 4000, the gate fails naming the file, measurement,\nbudget and 930B overage, exit 1; restored to 5632, it passes with 702B\nheadroom.\n\nKeeps the original raise argument in both bundle-budgets.json and ADR\n0009 rather than deleting it. A policy that preserves only the raises it\nstill agrees with preserves nothing, and the withdrawn argument is now\nalso a worked example of its own stated limit: a measured bound on the\nfixes you thought to look for is not a bound on the outcomes available.\n\nADR 0009 also warns against citing this budget as a guard on the\nCritical -- the test that holds it closed is\napps/console/src/federated/register.test.ts.","tree":{"sha":"4e0a51cdc707ffd39db38cf36f29dacd799c750d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/4e0a51cdc707ffd39db38cf36f29dacd799c750d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e0a51cdc707ffd39db38cf36f29dacd799c750d\nparent e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788217984 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788217984 +0700\n\nfix(gates): withdraw M6''s console bundle budget raise, restoring 5632\n\nRe-measured at e9c72dc, apps/console''s entry chunk is 4930B gzipped --\nunder the original 5632B budget, which is also the number the recorded\nrule regenerates from the new measurement (ceil(4930/1024)*1024 = 5120,\n*1.1 = 5632). M6 therefore ships no budget raise at all.\n\nNothing was optimised for size. The entry shrank as a side effect of the\nfinal review''s Critical fix: installing @sentra/flags in console''s\nfederated entry gave the flags runtime a second importer alongside\nmain.ts, so Rollup hoisted it out of the entry into the shared\nfederated-*.js chunk, which has no glob budget and is covered by\n$total:js.\n\nVerified in the built output rather than inferred from the byte drop --\na 968B fall is equally consistent with ''the runtime moved'' and with\n''something was dropped''. ''orders.bulkActions'' and fnv1a''s offset basis\n2166136261 appear in federated-*.js and in neither case in index-*.js;\nui.dataTable.sortBy appears in index-*.js and not in federated-*.js. So\nthe catalogue never moved and the locale analysis still holds -- it is\nsimply no longer load-bearing, because the 266B overage it explained is\ngone.\n\nFalsified the restored budget rather than trusting a green run:\ntemporarily set to 4000, the gate fails naming the file, measurement,\nbudget and 930B overage, exit 1; restored to 5632, it passes with 702B\nheadroom.\n\nKeeps the original raise argument in both bundle-budgets.json and ADR\n0009 rather than deleting it. A policy that preserves only the raises it\nstill agrees with preserves nothing, and the withdrawn argument is now\nalso a worked example of its own stated limit: a measured bound on the\nfixes you thought to look for is not a bound on the outcomes available.\n\nADR 0009 also warns against citing this budget as a guard on the\nCritical -- the test that holds it closed is\napps/console/src/federated/register.test.ts.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapYKgBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmJRvQEAnNndkq3cJZ36y0VcWXPf\nK6zrjic9lb7ocdYxA8jCFiwBAJM+qkmAuO4ZrHboXwFKPSXO6/LmI8JHcO2zbPsV\n7F0B\n=Ba8+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDcwNDNkMTBjN2M2YzVmODJlNDNjNGZlMzA2YmRjMDFhYzQ4Y2UyNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e","sha":"e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e"}],"sha":"7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/7043d10c7c6c5f82e43c4fe306bdc01ac48ce24d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:24:53Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:24:53Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"test(plugin-errors): assert the report carries a stack, not just the message\n\nThe final review''s finding I4 gap 1 was closed with\nexpect(reports[0]?.stack).toContain(''boom''), but a V8 stack begins with\n\"Error: boom\", so that assertion also passes when describe() copies\nmessage into stack -- the exact bug an assertion on stack exists to\ncatch. Verified: mutating reporter.ts:34''s stack: error.stack to\nstack: error.message left all 12 tests in reporter.test.ts green.\n\nAdds expect(...).toMatch(/\\n\\s+at /), which asserts stack structure and\nis unsatisfiable by a message. Falsified: with the same mutation the new\nline goes red at reporter.test.ts:35 while line 34''s toContain(''boom'')\nstill passes, so the added assertion is the load-bearing one. Reverted\nwith git checkout; git status --porcelain showed only the test file.\n\nAlso records in the comment that the mutation additionally turns\nreport.test.ts''s fingerprintOf case red, because the fingerprint derives\nfrom the stack. That is incidental coverage of a different unit, so the\ngap was a weak assertion here rather than a bug that could have shipped\nunnoticed -- worth stating precisely rather than overstating the\nseverity.","tree":{"sha":"28a76b11c7718e529d0f74b4f228cebedb0ba452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/28a76b11c7718e529d0f74b4f228cebedb0ba452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e","verification":{"payload":"tree 28a76b11c7718e529d0f74b4f228cebedb0ba452\nparent 2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788200693 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788200693 +0700\n\ntest(plugin-errors): assert the report carries a stack, not just the message\n\nThe final review''s finding I4 gap 1 was closed with\nexpect(reports[0]?.stack).toContain(''boom''), but a V8 stack begins with\n\"Error: boom\", so that assertion also passes when describe() copies\nmessage into stack -- the exact bug an assertion on stack exists to\ncatch. Verified: mutating reporter.ts:34''s stack: error.stack to\nstack: error.message left all 12 tests in reporter.test.ts green.\n\nAdds expect(...).toMatch(/\\n\\s+at /), which asserts stack structure and\nis unsatisfiable by a message. Falsified: with the same mutation the new\nline goes red at reporter.test.ts:35 while line 34''s toContain(''boom'')\nstill passes, so the added assertion is the load-bearing one. Reverted\nwith git checkout; git status --porcelain showed only the test file.\n\nAlso records in the comment that the mutation additionally turns\nreport.test.ts''s fingerprintOf case red, because the fingerprint derives\nfrom the stack. That is incidental coverage of a different unit, so the\ngap was a weak assertion here rather than a bug that could have shipped\nunnoticed -- worth stating precisely rather than overstating the\nseverity.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapXG9RsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmIlQAD/UTRoWd0qCatGLwqEWSdt\nIlwEwWXyViBSOeMdX15pzqsBAKHZ1BCceyYYrBpaJaJY4O355vrTn4EiLkVGjaeY\nXXwD\n=2STV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKGU5YzcyZGMwODI5YjQxY2Q5ZjFjNWJjMDlkMzhkODZkN2U1ZmE1NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622","sha":"2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622"}],"sha":"e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/e9c72dc0829b41cd9f1c5bc09d38d86d7e5fa55e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:13:57Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:13:57Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(m6): close final-review findings C1, I1-I4, M1-M2\n\nC1 (Critical) — apps/console/src/federated/register.ts never installed\n@sentra/flags: the federated console remote wired toast/ops plugins but\nnever called `createFlagClient`/`app.use(flagsPlugin, ...)`, so every\n`useFlags()` call in the federated build silently resolved to `NULL_FLAGS`\n(isOn always false) with no error. No existing flags test caught this\nbecause every prior test constructs a flag client directly, never through\na Vue app''s federated registration path. Fixed by mirroring main.ts''s\nstandalone wiring: build the flag client from CONSOLE_FLAGS + an ops-backed\nsource inside registerConsole, install it via app.use, and kick off\nrefresh(). Added apps/console/src/federated/register.test.ts, which stubs\nglobal fetch (the ops client''s real transport seam) rather than @sentra/flags\nitself, boots a real app through registerConsole, and asserts\nuseFlags().isOn(''orders.bulkActions'') is true after refresh — the strongest\nproof NULL_FLAGS was not silently resolved. Verified red against the\nunmodified register.ts (AssertionError: expected false to be true, failing\nat the isOn assertion after flushPromises), green after the fix.\n\nI1 — packages/flags/src/sources.ts httpSource() embedded the request URL\nin its thrown error message, which propagates through onError into the\nerror-reporting pipeline. redact() only scrubs by shape (query strings,\nemails, bearer tokens, long digit runs); it does not recognize the app''s\nown path-segment tokens, so a URL like `/v1/token/<token>/flags` could\nleak in an ADR-0012 \"best-effort\" report. Changed the message to a fixed,\ngeneric `httpSource: request failed with status ${response.status}` that\nnever carries `url` or the response body, matching the discipline\napps/console/src/flags.ts''s createOpsFlagSource already followed. Added a\ntest asserting the thrown message contains neither the host nor a\nrepresentative path-segment token, only the status code.\n\nI2 — packages/i18n/src/core.ts''s CLDR plural-branch selection had no test\nthat could distinguish a correct Intl.PluralRules(locale) selection from a\nhardcoded ''en''/''other'' fallback, because id.json lacks a ''one'' branch and\nthe existing en-only tests can''t tell \"selected via locale\" from \"landed\non the same branch by luck\". Added a test using a locale (ar) that CLDR\ngives a \"two\" branch English does not have; confirmed genuine locale-drive\nvia a throwaway `node -e` check of Intl.PluralRules(''ar'') vs (''en'') at\ncount:2. Falsifiability: temporarily hardcoded `rules = new\nIntl.PluralRules(''en'')` in selectPlural — the new test went red (returned\nthe ''other'' branch instead of ''two''); reverted, `git status --porcelain`\nclean.\n\nI3 — packages/flags/src/bucket.ts''s fnv1a() had tests only for shape\n(non-negative, deterministic, distributive) that any consistent hash\nsatisfies, not a check against the actual FNV-1a-32 constants. Since\nindex.ts already exports fnv1a publicly, pinned two independently-verified\npublished FNV-1a-32 reference vectors (fnv1a('''') = 0x811c9dc5, fnv1a(''a'')\n= 0xe40c292c) computed via a standalone script, not the codebase''s own\nimplementation. Falsifiability: changed the offset basis constant from\n0x811c9dc5 to 0x811c9dc6 — both new tests went red; reverted, clean status.\n\nI4 — packages/plugin-errors test-suite gaps (no production code changed):\n(1) reporter.test.ts''s \"reports an Error with its message and stack\" only\nasserted the message; added an assertion that the natural Error.stack\ncontains ''boom''. (2) \"survives a sink that throws\" didn''t confirm the\nreporter''s own count stayed consistent after the sink threw; added\n`expect(reporter.count).toBe(0)`. (3) sources.test.ts''s \"captures a window\nerror\" only asserted kind, so a bug swapping event.error for event.message\nin onError would pass; added a message assertion. (4) the single\n\"stops capturing after teardown\" test asserted all four source types\nsequentially, so a failure on the first source would mask whether the\nother three teardown paths worked at all; split into four independent\ntests, one per source.\n\nM1 — apps/storefront/src/i18n/index.ts''s missingTranslationError() had\ncorrect key/interpolation-parameter branch logic and zero test coverage;\nan inverted split or swapped branches would have gone unnoticed. Exported\nthe function (previously module-private) per the brief, and added direct\ntests for both branches plus tests confirming createStorefrontI18n''s\nonMissing hook wires actual missing-key and missing-interpolation-param\ncases through it with the expected {key, locale} context.\n\nM2 — scripts/check-catalogues.mjs had two gaps: (1) it only checked parity\nbetween whichever locales were present, so a stray locale (e.g. fr.json)\nthat happened to parity-check against en would pass, even though only\nen/id ship; added an ALLOWED_LOCALES allowlist check. (2) the plural-branch\ncheck gated on `typeof message === ''object''`, so a translation replacing a\nplural-shaped key with a plain string (or vice versa) was silently skipped\nrather than flagged; added an explicit shape-mismatch check. Added three\ntests covering the disallowed-locale case and both shape-mismatch\ndirections; no real fixture file was mutated for these (the new tests use\ninline objects), so no mutate/revert cycle applies to them. Re-ran the\nlive `pnpm verify:catalogues` gate against the repository''s real\ncatalogues: still passes (2 groups consistent).\n\nOut of scope per the fix-wave brief: I5 and M3 are untouched.\n\nGates run before this commit, all green: typecheck (turbo run typecheck,\n19/19 tasks); full unit suite (turbo run test && vitest run) — per package:\nconfig 9, sdk-ops 40, i18n 29, tokens 32, plugin-errors 41, result 3,\nshell-contract 29, ui 147, flags 42, console 20, sdk-commerce 128,\nplugin-analytics 21, storefront 109, shell 44, root scripts/*.test.mjs 151;\nverify:catalogues (2 groups consistent); format:check (clean after\n`pnpm format` reformatted two of this wave''s own new test files —\nprettier line-wrap only, re-verified with a targeted re-run of both files\npost-format).","tree":{"sha":"8b405140162305057f04cb4c322e557f1ff73df8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/8b405140162305057f04cb4c322e557f1ff73df8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b405140162305057f04cb4c322e557f1ff73df8\nparent 88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788200037 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788200037 +0700\n\nfix(m6): close final-review findings C1, I1-I4, M1-M2\n\nC1 (Critical) — apps/console/src/federated/register.ts never installed\n@sentra/flags: the federated console remote wired toast/ops plugins but\nnever called `createFlagClient`/`app.use(flagsPlugin, ...)`, so every\n`useFlags()` call in the federated build silently resolved to `NULL_FLAGS`\n(isOn always false) with no error. No existing flags test caught this\nbecause every prior test constructs a flag client directly, never through\na Vue app''s federated registration path. Fixed by mirroring main.ts''s\nstandalone wiring: build the flag client from CONSOLE_FLAGS + an ops-backed\nsource inside registerConsole, install it via app.use, and kick off\nrefresh(). Added apps/console/src/federated/register.test.ts, which stubs\nglobal fetch (the ops client''s real transport seam) rather than @sentra/flags\nitself, boots a real app through registerConsole, and asserts\nuseFlags().isOn(''orders.bulkActions'') is true after refresh — the strongest\nproof NULL_FLAGS was not silently resolved. Verified red against the\nunmodified register.ts (AssertionError: expected false to be true, failing\nat the isOn assertion after flushPromises), green after the fix.\n\nI1 — packages/flags/src/sources.ts httpSource() embedded the request URL\nin its thrown error message, which propagates through onError into the\nerror-reporting pipeline. redact() only scrubs by shape (query strings,\nemails, bearer tokens, long digit runs); it does not recognize the app''s\nown path-segment tokens, so a URL like `/v1/token/<token>/flags` could\nleak in an ADR-0012 \"best-effort\" report. Changed the message to a fixed,\ngeneric `httpSource: request failed with status ${response.status}` that\nnever carries `url` or the response body, matching the discipline\napps/console/src/flags.ts''s createOpsFlagSource already followed. Added a\ntest asserting the thrown message contains neither the host nor a\nrepresentative path-segment token, only the status code.\n\nI2 — packages/i18n/src/core.ts''s CLDR plural-branch selection had no test\nthat could distinguish a correct Intl.PluralRules(locale) selection from a\nhardcoded ''en''/''other'' fallback, because id.json lacks a ''one'' branch and\nthe existing en-only tests can''t tell \"selected via locale\" from \"landed\non the same branch by luck\". Added a test using a locale (ar) that CLDR\ngives a \"two\" branch English does not have; confirmed genuine locale-drive\nvia a throwaway `node -e` check of Intl.PluralRules(''ar'') vs (''en'') at\ncount:2. Falsifiability: temporarily hardcoded `rules = new\nIntl.PluralRules(''en'')` in selectPlural — the new test went red (returned\nthe ''other'' branch instead of ''two''); reverted, `git status --porcelain`\nclean.\n\nI3 — packages/flags/src/bucket.ts''s fnv1a() had tests only for shape\n(non-negative, deterministic, distributive) that any consistent hash\nsatisfies, not a check against the actual FNV-1a-32 constants. Since\nindex.ts already exports fnv1a publicly, pinned two independently-verified\npublished FNV-1a-32 reference vectors (fnv1a('''') = 0x811c9dc5, fnv1a(''a'')\n= 0xe40c292c) computed via a standalone script, not the codebase''s own\nimplementation. Falsifiability: changed the offset basis constant from\n0x811c9dc5 to 0x811c9dc6 — both new tests went red; reverted, clean status.\n\nI4 — packages/plugin-errors test-suite gaps (no production code changed):\n(1) reporter.test.ts''s \"reports an Error with its message and stack\" only\nasserted the message; added an assertion that the natural Error.stack\ncontains ''boom''. (2) \"survives a sink that throws\" didn''t confirm the\nreporter''s own count stayed consistent after the sink threw; added\n`expect(reporter.count).toBe(0)`. (3) sources.test.ts''s \"captures a window\nerror\" only asserted kind, so a bug swapping event.error for event.message\nin onError would pass; added a message assertion. (4) the single\n\"stops capturing after teardown\" test asserted all four source types\nsequentially, so a failure on the first source would mask whether the\nother three teardown paths worked at all; split into four independent\ntests, one per source.\n\nM1 — apps/storefront/src/i18n/index.ts''s missingTranslationError() had\ncorrect key/interpolation-parameter branch logic and zero test coverage;\nan inverted split or swapped branches would have gone unnoticed. Exported\nthe function (previously module-private) per the brief, and added direct\ntests for both branches plus tests confirming createStorefrontI18n''s\nonMissing hook wires actual missing-key and missing-interpolation-param\ncases through it with the expected {key, locale} context.\n\nM2 — scripts/check-catalogues.mjs had two gaps: (1) it only checked parity\nbetween whichever locales were present, so a stray locale (e.g. fr.json)\nthat happened to parity-check against en would pass, even though only\nen/id ship; added an ALLOWED_LOCALES allowlist check. (2) the plural-branch\ncheck gated on `typeof message === ''object''`, so a translation replacing a\nplural-shaped key with a plain string (or vice versa) was silently skipped\nrather than flagged; added an explicit shape-mismatch check. Added three\ntests covering the disallowed-locale case and both shape-mismatch\ndirections; no real fixture file was mutated for these (the new tests use\ninline objects), so no mutate/revert cycle applies to them. Re-ran the\nlive `pnpm verify:catalogues` gate against the repository''s real\ncatalogues: still passes (2 groups consistent).\n\nOut of scope per the fix-wave brief: I5 and M3 are untouched.\n\nGates run before this commit, all green: typecheck (turbo run typecheck,\n19/19 tasks); full unit suite (turbo run test && vitest run) — per package:\nconfig 9, sdk-ops 40, i18n 29, tokens 32, plugin-errors 41, result 3,\nshell-contract 29, ui 147, flags 42, console 20, sdk-commerce 128,\nplugin-analytics 21, storefront 109, shell 44, root scripts/*.test.mjs 151;\nverify:catalogues (2 groups consistent); format:check (clean after\n`pnpm format` reformatted two of this wave''s own new test files —\nprettier line-wrap only, re-verified with a targeted re-run of both files\npost-format).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapXEZRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmL0iwEA25ugAJk9CzPNPZfaU4mb\n9JIdCJVqEGztTPRToIDXElUA/3ag995QNPSvI4lfEVBVyFmlcpzfZYlPVlS9Kq9b\nnQcO\n=8/et\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDJiNThhMTUxMDM4NmZlYzU0MzQ0ZDg0MDJmY2M5YzQ0NGY3Mzk2MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634","sha":"88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634"}],"sha":"2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/2b58a1510386fec54344d8402fcc9c444f739622"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:29:45Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:29:45Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs: state the budget-raise argument as a measured bound, not an exhaustive search\n\nThe scoped re-review confirmed both Important findings addressed and\nraised one Minor against the correction itself: it called removing the\nIndonesian catalogue \"the most aggressive locale-side fix available\",\nwhich reads as exhaustive while the record showed only one candidate\ntested.\n\nThe claim survived the reviewer''s attack, but the objection is right\nabout the record. A second candidate does exist and was never named:\ncurating the catalogue''s contents rather than its locales. Console''s own\nviews reference only DataTable (OrdersView.vue:5), three of the\ncatalogue''s seven keys.\n\nThat candidate is capped twice over. en.json is also a single JSON object\nliteral, so unused keys inside it are no more droppable than an unused\nlocale is; and four keys of seven cannot exceed the 134 bytes the entire\nother half of the catalogue costs. Whether Toast''s and Combobox''s keys\nreach the chunk through @sentra/ui''s barrel export regardless is flagged\nas a separate, unmeasured question rather than asserted either way.\n\nBoth files now state a bound on the two available fixes instead of\nclaiming no other fix could exist. That is the weaker claim, and the only\none the measurements support.\n\nNo budget number changes. JSON revalidated, verify:bundle-size and\nformat:check pass.","tree":{"sha":"d2ad8aa2e45ffc0afb10318db12b5ccbe6324d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/d2ad8aa2e45ffc0afb10318db12b5ccbe6324d4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634","verification":{"payload":"tree d2ad8aa2e45ffc0afb10318db12b5ccbe6324d4c\nparent 96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788197385 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788197385 +0700\n\ndocs: state the budget-raise argument as a measured bound, not an exhaustive search\n\nThe scoped re-review confirmed both Important findings addressed and\nraised one Minor against the correction itself: it called removing the\nIndonesian catalogue \"the most aggressive locale-side fix available\",\nwhich reads as exhaustive while the record showed only one candidate\ntested.\n\nThe claim survived the reviewer''s attack, but the objection is right\nabout the record. A second candidate does exist and was never named:\ncurating the catalogue''s contents rather than its locales. Console''s own\nviews reference only DataTable (OrdersView.vue:5), three of the\ncatalogue''s seven keys.\n\nThat candidate is capped twice over. en.json is also a single JSON object\nliteral, so unused keys inside it are no more droppable than an unused\nlocale is; and four keys of seven cannot exceed the 134 bytes the entire\nother half of the catalogue costs. Whether Toast''s and Combobox''s keys\nreach the chunk through @sentra/ui''s barrel export regardless is flagged\nas a separate, unmeasured question rather than asserted either way.\n\nBoth files now state a bound on the two available fixes instead of\nclaiming no other fix could exist. That is the weaker claim, and the only\none the measurements support.\n\nNo budget number changes. JSON revalidated, verify:bundle-size and\nformat:check pass.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapW6CRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmIhZwD/TzPYBsjjzxppaS/BdGlS\nXHCVrzKboNp7NS8lCxqZJhcA/jrYkxn1WgFhC//pO31SUkdHqrJn42o+1/pPKkP+\nqT8C\n=bWXs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDg4NjEzOTU0YmVhY2ExNDdhNzcwMTI0ZDcyNTkwYzA0MTZkYjE2MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0","sha":"96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0"}],"sha":"88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/88613954beaca147a770124d72590c0416db1634"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:18:00Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:18:00Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs: correct the recorded cause of the console budget raise\n\nThe budget raise in 13cfcd7 was justified with two false claims, both\ncaught by the Task 15 review.\n\nFirst, it said the console received \"its own en/id catalogues\" that\nmain.ts imports statically. It has none -- apps/console/src/i18n does\nnot exist, and main.ts:127 installs @sentra/ui''s shared uiMessages. The\nfile''s own JSDoc at main.ts:117-118 already said so.\n\nSecond, it cited ADR 0011''s exclusion of lazy per-locale catalogue\nsplitting as the reason no code fix was available. Dropping a locale the\napp never selects is dead-code elimination, not lazy loading, so that\nexclusion did not apply to the fix actually on the table.\n\nThe corrected record replaces the inference with a measurement, taken at\nthis tree: uiMessages is one object literal, so installing\n{ en: uiMessages.en } still constructs the whole object and saves 5\nbytes; removing id from the shared package brings the entry to 5764B,\nstill 132B over the 5632B budget, because id.json''s 254B standalone gzip\ncosts only 134B inside a chunk where en has already primed the\ndictionary. No locale-side fix closes a 266B overage, which is what\nmakes the raise the honest remedy rather than the convenient one.\n\nCommitted as a correction rather than an amend so both the error and its\nfix stay in the history -- ADR 0009 requires a raise to leave a record a\nlater reader can disagree with, and a record that quietly rewrites its\nown mistakes does not qualify.\n\nNo budget number changes: console assets/index-*.js stays at 6759, and a\nforced rebuild re-measures the entry at 5898B. verify:bundle-size and\nformat:check pass.","tree":{"sha":"82005e021a1d7dd59ed84cb92cf8a585d59fca31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/82005e021a1d7dd59ed84cb92cf8a585d59fca31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 82005e021a1d7dd59ed84cb92cf8a585d59fca31\nparent 13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788196680 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788196680 +0700\n\ndocs: correct the recorded cause of the console budget raise\n\nThe budget raise in 13cfcd7 was justified with two false claims, both\ncaught by the Task 15 review.\n\nFirst, it said the console received \"its own en/id catalogues\" that\nmain.ts imports statically. It has none -- apps/console/src/i18n does\nnot exist, and main.ts:127 installs @sentra/ui''s shared uiMessages. The\nfile''s own JSDoc at main.ts:117-118 already said so.\n\nSecond, it cited ADR 0011''s exclusion of lazy per-locale catalogue\nsplitting as the reason no code fix was available. Dropping a locale the\napp never selects is dead-code elimination, not lazy loading, so that\nexclusion did not apply to the fix actually on the table.\n\nThe corrected record replaces the inference with a measurement, taken at\nthis tree: uiMessages is one object literal, so installing\n{ en: uiMessages.en } still constructs the whole object and saves 5\nbytes; removing id from the shared package brings the entry to 5764B,\nstill 132B over the 5632B budget, because id.json''s 254B standalone gzip\ncosts only 134B inside a chunk where en has already primed the\ndictionary. No locale-side fix closes a 266B overage, which is what\nmakes the raise the honest remedy rather than the convenient one.\n\nCommitted as a correction rather than an amend so both the error and its\nfix stay in the history -- ADR 0009 requires a raise to leave a record a\nlater reader can disagree with, and a record that quietly rewrites its\nown mistakes does not qualify.\n\nNo budget number changes: console assets/index-*.js stays at 6759, and a\nforced rebuild re-measures the entry at 5898B. verify:bundle-size and\nformat:check pass.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapW3SBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLhgAEA7nD12kDxvCOv94w1v/RU\nSA6GsClw1JqqHT9gingCROsA/0MGBGfEN/MTOK1CH5bLPx7OTvdNoHXBLBXrIJsd\nHaAH\n=KTQu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDk2YTI2YzJiYWRjMmVkZWExZDA2ZWFiZDY2ZTM2MzVmMzdmZjg4YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2","sha":"13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2"}],"sha":"96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96a26c2badc2edea1d06eabd66e3635f37ff88c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:59:23Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:59:23Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"chore(gates): raise console''s entry budget to its measured cost and record why\n\nM6 wires @sentra/i18n, @sentra/plugin-errors and @sentra/flags into apps/console\nand adds its en/id catalogues, which main.ts imports statically. The entry chunk\nmeasures 5898B gzipped against a 5632B budget calibrated on 2026-08-30, so\nverify:bundle-size fails.\n\nRaise that one key to 6759B by the rule bundle-budgets.json already states\n(ceil(5898/1024)*1024 = 6144, *1.1 = 6758.4, fractional byte up), record the\nmeasurement with the commit it was taken at, and name the cause. A code fix was\nrejected: the only one available is splitting the catalogues out of the entry\nchunk, which ADR 0011 places outside M6''s scope.\n\nADR 0009 gains the policy this follows -- a raise must be derived by the stated\nrule, recorded with its commit, and have its cause named, so a later reader can\ndisagree with it. Exactly one key moved; shell and storefront entries grew too\n(4220->5178, 4814->5156) and still fit, so both now sit within 500B of the same\nbudget.","tree":{"sha":"44108faed331960f1d08ff3d254d579b74512bfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/44108faed331960f1d08ff3d254d579b74512bfd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/13cfcd7aa3b0e44fc9f0eeb7cd9b59bcf8c7a5f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 44108faed331960f1d08ff3d254d579b74512bfd\nparent f2f1e2401a37756bd6b3b42247484b6d4753e029\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788195563 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788195563 +0700\n\nchore(gates): raise console''s entry budget to its measured cost and record why\n\nM6 wires @sentra/i18n, @sentra/plugin-errors and @sentra/flags into apps/console\nand adds its en/id catalogues, which main.ts imports statically. The entry chunk\nmeasures 5898B gzipped against a 5632B budget calibrated on 2026-08-30, so\nverify:bundle-size fails.\n\nRaise that one key to 6759B by the rule bundle-budgets.json already states\n(ceil(5898/1024)*1024 = 6144, *1.1 = 6758.4, fractional byte up), record the\nmeasurement with the commit it was taken at, and name the cause. A code fix was\nrejected: the only one available is splitting the catalogues out of the entry\nchunk, which ADR 0011 places outside M6''s scope.\n\nADR 0009 gains the policy this follows -- a raise must be derived by the stated\nrule, recorded with its commit, and have its cause named, so a later reader can\ndisagree with it. Exactly one key moved; shell and storefront entries grew too\n(4220->5178, 4814->5156) and still fit, so both now sit within 500B of the same\nbudget.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapWy6xsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLN7QEAsGjQ0DWa/q9fNjRNfIKV\nIYtqmBUKyEnjTQJm3Pw1FisA/i0dKjhnPW/69m1fzpMjFdZ8MEjFSjw30DlX4REd\nYwkE\n=CUmn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T00:03:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_