hub.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a68b8afc398328a5a2bc76840c994da55e079fd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:39:57Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:39:57Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"feat(ui): translate the library''s five user-facing strings\n\nRoutes @sentra/ui''s five hardcoded user-facing strings (ToastHost''s\ndismiss label, DataTable''s sort/empty/scrollable-region labels, and\nCombobox''s loading text) through useI18n(), and ships en/id catalogues\nplus a typed uiMessages boundary in packages/ui/src/i18n/.\n\nTwo pre-existing tests asserted on literal English text that useI18n()\nnow resolves through NULL_I18N (raw key, no interpolation) when no\ni18n is installed:\n\n- DataTable.test.ts''s \"labels the table and its scrollable region for\n  assistive technology\" now expects the raw key\n  ''ui.dataTable.rowsScrollable'' instead of the interpolated string.\n- DataTable.test.ts''s \"emits a sort request from a sortable header,\n  toggling direction\" now queries the sort button by the raw key\n  ''ui.dataTable.sortBy'' instead of matching \"sort by name\".\n\nBoth are translated to the raw key rather than reintroducing the\nliteral, preserving coverage of the null-object path that every\n@sentra/ui consumer and Storybook story relies on. Sibling tests\n(installing i18n) prove the actual translations.","tree":{"sha":"b7a3ea20746b3d668fee4e339bcfc7a815c54ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/b7a3ea20746b3d668fee4e339bcfc7a815c54ef2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/a68b8afc398328a5a2bc76840c994da55e079fd7","verification":{"payload":"tree b7a3ea20746b3d668fee4e339bcfc7a815c54ef2\npa