llowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a3f3f3646eff7a17b7bb4f743111b76e428c6281/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:46:41Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:46:41Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(storefront): stop Tailwind emitting utilities named only in tests\n\nTailwind''s source scanner reads raw text; it does not parse TypeScript, so\nit cannot tell a class name a component uses from one a test names in order\nto forbid it. `motion.test.ts` exists to fail any preset that reaches for\n`ease-in-out`, `ease-linear`, `ease-in`, `ease-out` or `duration-200` — and\nby naming them, it was the sole reason all five shipped to users as real CSS\nrules. The guard against a utility was what put that utility in the bundle.\n\nExcluding `*.test.ts` from the scan removes 499 bytes of raw CSS (83 gzipped)\nand, with it, the Lighthouse stylesheet-budget failure the motion commit\nintroduced. The exclusion is written against the file pattern rather than\nthose five names because the mechanism is general: any assertion about a\nclass name, present or future, would otherwise emit it.\n\nThe same scanner still emits `.collapse` from the English word \"collapse\" in\na prose comment. That is the same mechanism at 19 bytes, and it is not\nfixable without giving up source scanning; it is noted here so the exclusion\nabove is not mistaken for a complete defence.","tree":{"sha":"84a44d798788fcc19f9922b11b86627a89eec7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/84a44d798788fcc19f9922b11b86627a89eec7d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/a3f3f3646eff7a17b7bb4f743111b76e428c6281","verification":{"payload":"tree 84a44d798788fcc19f9922b11b86627a89eec7d0\nparent a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788112001 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788112001 +0700\n\nfix(storefront): stop Tailwind emitting utilities named only in tests\n\nTailwind''s source scanner reads raw text; it does not parse TypeScript, so\nit cannot tell a class name a component uses from one a test names in order\nto forbid it. `motion.test.ts` exists to fail any preset that reaches for\n`ease-in-out`, `ease-linear`, `ease-in`, `ease-out` or `duration-200` — and\nby naming them, it was the sole reason all five shipped to users as real CSS\nrules. The guard against a utility was what put that utility in the bundle.\n\nExcluding `*.test.ts` from the scan removes 499 bytes of raw CSS (83 gzipped)\nand, with it, the Lighthouse stylesheet-budget failure the motion commit\nintroduced. The exclusion is written against the file pattern rather than\nthose five names because the mechanism is general: any assertion about a\nclass name, present or future, would otherwise emit it.\n\nThe same scanner still emits `.collapse` from the English word \"collapse\" in\na prose comment. That is the same mechanism at 19 bytes, and it is not\nfixable without giving up source scanning; it is noted here so the exclusion\nabove is not mistaken for a complete defence.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapRsgRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLCCAEAmQfj2yByODPi2YM7nMlB\nWD2PDRhT4gumSpupHRY9dpQA/1NeojkAG7NotgQt9TmV3ObkP4EMRhXzNUKeVOQs\n90UC\n=MJBi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T17:46:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/a3f3f3646eff7a17b7bb4f743111b76e428c6281","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKGEzZjNmMzY0NmVmZjdhMTdiN2JiNGY3NDMxMTFiNzZlNDI4YzYyODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865","sha":"a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865"}],"sha":"a3f3f3646eff7a17b7bb4f743111b76e428c6281","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a3f3f3646eff7a17b7bb4f743111b76e428c6281"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:24:47Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:24:47Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"feat(storybook): brand the manager with the Sentra mark and wordmark\n\nAdds a manager theme that renders the mark next to \"SENTRA\" in the sidebar\nand puts the mark in the browser tab. Accent and radius are read from\n@sentra/tokens rather than retyped as literals, so the documentation of the\nbrand cannot drift from the brand.\n\nThe supplied logo was a JPEG with the transparency checkerboard baked in as\nopaque pixels. It is keyed out by chroma — the mark is entirely saturated,\nthe checker entirely achromatic — and un-premultiplied against white so the\ncut-out carries no pale halo onto a dark background. The result is one 256px\nPNG shared by the sidebar, the favicon, and the README header.\n\nAlso paints the preview canvas from --color-neutral-50 in the existing theme\ndecorator. The canvas previously kept the manager''s colour while the stories\non it switched, so a dark-mode story was documented on a white page.","tree":{"sha":"7905f1f74dfff59e9640d0a1b9f79de8f4c64fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/7905f1f74dfff59e9640d0a1b9f79de8f4c64fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865","verification":{"payload":"tree 7905f1f74dfff59e9640d0a1b9f79de8f4c64fa6\nparent 7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788110687 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788110687 +0700\n\nfeat(storybook): brand the manager with the Sentra mark and wordmark\n\nAdds a manager theme that renders the mark next to \"SENTRA\" in the sidebar\nand puts the mark in the browser tab. Accent and radius are read from\n@sentra/tokens rather than retyped as literals, so the documentation of the\nbrand cannot drift from the brand.\n\nThe supplied logo was a JPEG with the transparency checkerboard baked in as\nopaque pixels. It is keyed out by chroma — the mark is entirely saturated,\nthe checker entirely achromatic — and un-premultiplied against white so the\ncut-out carries no pale halo onto a dark background. The result is one 256px\nPNG shared by the sidebar, the favicon, and the README header.\n\nAlso paints the preview canvas from --color-neutral-50 in the existing theme\ndecorator. The canvas previously kept the manager''s colour while the stories\non it switched, so a dark-mode story was documented on a white page.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapRnXxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmJgvQEAoSL2vn7wAnxZ6XVWznrf\ndtgW/zMrheu9NtMYItT6hJUA/2WDiW5LyEG0a+TYdOwZL59AwlFTwhTTrY6JiA+J\nwjcE\n=3MUD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T17:38:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKGE5YzkzN2RmYjVmMGIwMTA1NWUwZGUwYmM0MTVlNWFhYzYwYjg4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec","sha":"7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec"}],"sha":"a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/a9c937dfb5f0b01055e0de0bc415e5aac60b8865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:53:19Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:53:19Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"feat(motion): token-driven transitions with a reduced-motion mode\n\nOverlays appeared and disappeared between frames. The duration tokens\nexisted from M1 with no consumers, and css.ts already whitelisted `ease`\nas a Tailwind namespace, so this finishes a declared token category\nrather than adding a new one.\n\n- tokens: add the `ease` branch (standard/enter/exit — role names, not\n  in/out/in-out, which would silently redefine Tailwind''s own utilities),\n  and `reducedMotionTokens`, emitted last so a user''s OS preference\n  outranks dark and compact at equal specificity.\n- ui: five `<Transition>` presets in shared/motion.ts, consumed by Dialog\n  (backdrop fade + drawer slide / modal scale), Combobox (popover), and\n  ToastHost (now a TransitionGroup, for the move transition). No preset\n  writes a millisecond value, which is what lets the token override\n  collapse everything to zero.\n- tests: unstub `<Transition>` — Vue Test Utils renders a real\n  `<transition-stub>` element, which had been quietly redefining what\n  `parentElement` meant for every transitioned child.\n- Dialog play functions now wait for the leave; a synchronous\n  `queryByRole` check passes in happy-dom and fails in a browser.\n\nADR 0010 records the mechanism and its one documented gap: Tailwind''s\n`animate-*` keyframe utilities set their own duration, so ProductCard''s\n`animate-pulse` skeleton is not reached by the override.","tree":{"sha":"8211417a525444917aaf39f8918618e751ebbb34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/8211417a525444917aaf39f8918618e751ebbb34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec","verification":{"payload":"tree 8211417a525444917aaf39f8918618e751ebbb34\nparent ca2ecf43b678496a7791875c3a95a61b0243e285\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788108799 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788108799 +0700\n\nfeat(motion): token-driven transitions with a reduced-motion mode\n\nOverlays appeared and disappeared between frames. The duration tokens\nexisted from M1 with no consumers, and css.ts already whitelisted `ease`\nas a Tailwind namespace, so this finishes a declared token category\nrather than adding a new one.\n\n- tokens: add the `ease` branch (standard/enter/exit — role names, not\n  in/out/in-out, which would silently redefine Tailwind''s own utilities),\n  and `reducedMotionTokens`, emitted last so a user''s OS preference\n  outranks dark and compact at equal specificity.\n- ui: five `<Transition>` presets in shared/motion.ts, consumed by Dialog\n  (backdrop fade + drawer slide / modal scale), Combobox (popover), and\n  ToastHost (now a TransitionGroup, for the move transition). No preset\n  writes a millisecond value, which is what lets the token override\n  collapse everything to zero.\n- tests: unstub `<Transition>` — Vue Test Utils renders a real\n  `<transition-stub>` element, which had been quietly redefining what\n  `parentElement` meant for every transitioned child.\n- Dialog play functions now wait for the leave; a synchronous\n  `queryByRole` check passes in happy-dom and fails in a browser.\n\nADR 0010 records the mechanism and its one documented gap: Tailwind''s\n`animate-*` keyframe utilities set their own duration, so ProductCard''s\n`animate-pulse` skeleton is not reached by the override.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapRf/xsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmKiXwEAoIkxaNwiZDkFUwilW/Xu\nsLWzoO4yLzJleIWuXTpS4XwBAKGRu9OSujcSCyZC9fnE/9E9mDzB7AuzaIpDVpLp\nWnkH\n=yq9K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T17:38:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3dcd1b4a9665b056113dec","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDdhYWUyYjJhNGUzZDQ3ZmI1ZjNkY2QxYjRhOTY2NWIwNTYxMTNkZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/ca2ecf43b678496a7791875c3a95a61b0243e285","sha":"ca2ecf43b678496a7791875c3a95a61b0243e285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/ca2ecf43b678496a7791875c3a95a61b0243e285"}],"sha":"7aae2b2a4e3d47fb5f3d