epos/barayuda/sentra/commits/797cbfbde87e67965fa7e75368a2c43889b77882"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/c4d0944f74dcbd808ab17994774c5a8ae715a637/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:10:35Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:10:35Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs(adr-0009): record the build-ordering hazard the DOM floor caught\n\n`pnpm test` rebuilds both remotes — `@sentra/shell#test` inherits `^build`\nthrough the `optionalDependencies` edge that exists so a stripped tree still\nresolves — while `@sentra/shell#build`, the only task that runs\n`hash-remotes.mjs`, is absent from that graph. The result is a tree whose\nremote bundles were built without VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS and whose shell manifest\npins digests for bundles that no longer exist.\n\nLighthouse scored performance 0.99 and accessibility 1 on the resulting\nfourteen-element page; every lhci assertion passed and the DOM floor was the\nonly failure. CI''s verify job already runs every dist-reading gate before\n`pnpm test`, so the hazard is local and no new CI gate is warranted — one\nwould have no reachable failing case there.","tree":{"sha":"85a556b483968db95f44be1814ebda16ead83684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/85a556b483968db95f44be1814ebda16ead83684"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/c4d0944f74dcbd808ab17994774c5a8ae715a637","verification":{"payload":"tree 85a556b483968db95f44be1814ebda16ead83684\nparent 37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788099035 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788099035 +0700\n\ndocs(adr-0009): record the build-ordering hazard the DOM floor caught\n\n`pnpm test` rebuilds both remotes — `@sentra/shell#test` inherits `^build`\nthrough the `optionalDependencies` edge that exists so a stripped tree still\nresolves — while `@sentra/shell#build`, the only task that runs\n`hash-remotes.mjs`, is absent from that graph. The result is a tree whose\nremote bundles were built without VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS and whose shell manifest\npins digests for bundles that no longer exist.\n\nLighthouse scored performance 0.99 and accessibility 1 on the resulting\nfourteen-element page; every lhci assertion passed and the DOM floor was the\nonly failure. CI''s verify job already runs every dist-reading gate before\n`pnpm test`, so the hazard is local and no new CI gate is warranted — one\nwould have no reachable failing case there.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQ52xsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmK4mAEAnzXgUl/og9r2/oHBHAOV\ngufZyHVh2tmNmntGgZ2XaYAA/1MFPTaVAo2yU4o9i1qxrlxPMAyN25yw4MNTblc6\ngLID\n=4vdR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/c4d0944f74dcbd808ab17994774c5a8ae715a637","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKGM0ZDA5NDRmNzRkY2JkODA4YWIxNzk5NDc3NGM1YThhZTcxNWE2Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c","sha":"37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c"}],"sha":"c4d0944f74dcbd808ab17994774c5a8ae715a637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/c4d0944f74dcbd808ab17994774c5a8ae715a637"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:50:26Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:50:26Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix: ship the console''s MSW worker and check that every app that starts one does\n\napps/console declared an init-msw script but the artifact it generates was\nnever committed, unlike apps/shell and apps/storefront. Without\npublic/mockServiceWorker.js the SPA fallback serves index.html for the worker\nrequest, the browser refuses to register a Service Worker delivered as\ntext/html, and because main.ts awaits startMockWorker() before createApp the\nwhole standalone app renders a blank page.\n\nNothing in CI covered it: the federation e2e runs console code inside the\nshell''s page where the shell''s worker already controls scope /, Lighthouse\nruns against the shell, and unit tests mock a layer below the worker. The\nconsole''s standalone mocked mode had no check at all.\n\nscripts/msw-worker.mjs derives the apps that import msw/browser from the\nworkspace, the same source of truth check-sourcemaps.mjs uses, so a stripped\nreference app is absent rather than reported missing. The real-tree test\nasserts the derived set is non-empty before asserting nothing is missing --\nwithout that line it would pass on a tree where the derivation broke.\nVerified load-bearing: removing the worker file turns exactly that one test\nred.","tree":{"sha":"dc39df8c7933a4af0a772a7ba0104ab8ed4943e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/dc39df8c7933a4af0a772a7ba0104ab8ed4943e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c","verification":{"payload":"tree dc39df8c7933a4af0a772a7ba0104ab8ed4943e8\nparent 96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788097826 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788097826 +0700\n\nfix: ship the console''s MSW worker and check that every app that starts one does\n\napps/console declared an init-msw script but the artifact it generates was\nnever committed, unlike apps/shell and apps/storefront. Without\npublic/mockServiceWorker.js the SPA fallback serves index.html for the worker\nrequest, the browser refuses to register a Service Worker delivered as\ntext/html, and because main.ts awaits startMockWorker() before createApp the\nwhole standalone app renders a blank page.\n\nNothing in CI covered it: the federation e2e runs console code inside the\nshell''s page where the shell''s worker already controls scope /, Lighthouse\nruns against the shell, and unit tests mock a layer below the worker. The\nconsole''s standalone mocked mode had no check at all.\n\nscripts/msw-worker.mjs derives the apps that import msw/browser from the\nworkspace, the same source of truth check-sourcemaps.mjs uses, so a stripped\nreference app is absent rather than reported missing. The real-tree test\nasserts the derived set is non-empty before asserting nothing is missing --\nwithout that line it would pass on a tree where the derivation broke.\nVerified load-bearing: removing the worker file turns exactly that one test\nred.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQ1IhsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmKSCgD/e8c3YWaSFmtLuw6JSc+y\neLl3GW1MPOHt5yqbw+gzQJsBAPNH8J7aGy7ot4PRHmtBfS4QJmmFie1t+XjOX3Nb\nTEsF\n=jKVn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDM3YmRmNjU3MmM2NDA2ZWNjNWVlNTkwZmQ0OGQ0YzJiYjMwYWQ2OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4","sha":"96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4"}],"sha":"37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/37bdf6572c6406ecc5ee590fd48d4c2bb30ad68c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:34:28Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:34:28Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix: make the sourcemap gate''s zero-app case and its test assertions load-bearing\n\nTwo refinements to the gate landed in 26e574e.\n\nmain() printed \"passed for N apps\" unconditionally, so a workspace\ndeclaring no apps under apps/ would print \"passed for 0 apps\" and exit\n0 — a loop over zero apps collects zero failures, which reads as a\ncontrol that ran when nothing was inspected. hash-remotes.mjs:85-90\nalready settled this shape for an empty remote manifest; this follows\nthat precedent with a distinct message, and still does not exit\nnon-zero because a workspace may legally contain no apps. Also fixes\nthe plural so a single app does not report \"1 apps\".\n\nThe stripped-tree test asserted that failures mentions neither\nstorefront nor console, one line after asserting failures is empty —\nan empty list mentions nothing, so both assertions held identically\nwhether or not the fix worked. Replaced with an assertion on apps, the\nvalue the fix actually changes. Verified load-bearing: reverting\nappsRequiringSourcemaps to the old hardcoded array turns it red.","tree":{"sha":"8ca6648f744d652b4349b494c5899c92b2977359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/8ca6648f744d652b4349b494c5899c92b2977359"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ca6648f744d652b4349b494c5899c92b2977359\nparent 26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788096868 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788096868 +0700\n\nfix: make the sourcemap gate''s zero-app case and its test assertions load-bearing\n\nTwo refinements to the gate landed in 26e574e.\n\nmain() printed \"passed for N apps\" unconditionally, so a workspace\ndeclaring no apps under apps/ would print \"passed for 0 apps\" and exit\n0 — a loop over zero apps collects zero failures, which reads as a\ncontrol that ran when nothing was inspected. hash-remotes.mjs:85-90\nalready settled this shape for an empty remote manifest; this follows\nthat precedent with a distinct message, and still does not exit\nnon-zero because a workspace may legally contain no apps. Also fixes\nthe plural so a single app does not report \"1 apps\".\n\nThe stripped-tree test asserted that failures mentions neither\nstorefront nor console, one line after asserting failures is empty —\nan empty list mentions nothing, so both assertions held identically\nwhether or not the fix worked. Replaced with an assertion on apps, the\nvalue the fix actually changes. Verified load-bearing: reverting\nappsRequiringSourcemaps to the old hardcoded array turns it red.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQxZBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLzxAEAnfYh5+tpl5bCBULelqC4\nk9e+zM16noqJ10XXxru1+t4BAM3XqMzmMFNWsyrMlMXH+7T7gRT/zSgUZflN+I0w\nFZ0I\n=m57j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDk2NDYwNjgyZTk3Y2RiZWQ3ZGE3ZTFiMDAxNGY5NDQyOTlhZGIyYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078","sha":"26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078"}],"sha":"96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/96460682e97cdbed7da7e1b0014f944299adb2b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:26:54Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:26:54Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix: derive sourcemap gate from workspace, widen doc no-numbers sweep\n\ncheck-sourcemaps.mjs hardcoded APPS = [storefront, console, shell], so\non a stripped platform-only tree it reported \"run the build first\" for\napps an adopter deliberately deleted via strip-reference.mjs, instead\nof staying silent about their absence. It now derives its app list from\nreadWorkspaceMembers (the same source of truth as workspace.mjs and\nstrip-reference.mjs), so an app absent from the workspace is silently\ncorrect while an app present but unbuilt still fails with the existing\nmessage. Adds check-sourcemaps.test.mjs, the one gate script that had\nno test file, covering: app selection from the live workspace, silence\nabout an absent reference app, pass/fail on built/missing dist output,\nand the stripped-tree case end to end. This file is pre-M5 (unchanged\nby this branch since main at c47a968) — this improves pre-existing\ncode, not an M5 regression.\n\ndocs/proposal/README.md''s no-numbers-in-prose sweep regex required the\nnumber and plural noun to be immediately adjacent, so it missed cases\nlike `eleven \"cannot find module\" errors` (punctuation intervenes) and\n`eighteen exported modules` (an adjective intervenes). Widens the\npattern to tolerate up to three intervening words and to recognise\nnumber words through \"twenty\", verified against both examples before\npublishing. Adds prose disclosing that the sweep also under-reports in\nthe opposite direction and that no regex closes that gap. Re-running\nthe widened sweep over README.md, docs/proposal, packages/*/README.md,\nand apps/*/README.md surfaced a small number of genuine stale-prone\ninventory counts, now reworded to drop the count while leaving\nlegitimate non-inventory prose (logical structure, anaphora, and\nclaims.md''s evidence-grounded C10) untouched.","tree":{"sha":"990da3e7dbcd53319295cbcd50caa65a3b4ad64a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/990da3e7dbcd53319295cbcd50caa65a3b4ad64a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078","verification":{"payload":"tree 990da3e7dbcd53319295cbcd50caa65a3b4ad64a\nparent 2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788096414 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788096414 +0700\n\nfix: derive sourcemap gate from workspace, widen doc no-numbers sweep\n\ncheck-sourcemaps.mjs hardcoded APPS = [storefront, console, shell], so\non a stripped platform-only tree it reported \"run the build first\" for\napps an adopter deliberately deleted via strip-reference.mjs, instead\nof staying silent about their absence. It now derives its app list from\nreadWorkspaceMembers (the same source of truth as workspace.mjs and\nstrip-reference.mjs), so an app absent from the workspace is silently\ncorrect while an app present but unbuilt still fails with the existing\nmessage. Adds check-sourcemaps.test.mjs, the one gate script that had\nno test file, covering: app selection from the live workspace, silence\nabout an absent reference app, pass/fail on built/missing dist output,\nand the stripped-tree case end to end. This file is pre-M5 (unchanged\nby this branch since main at c47a968) — this improves pre-existing\ncode, not an M5 regression.\n\ndocs/proposal/README.md''s no-numbers-in-prose sweep regex required the\nnumber and plural noun to be immediately adjacent, so it missed cases\nlike `eleven \"cannot find module\" errors` (punctuation intervenes) and\n`eighteen exported modules` (an adjective intervenes). Widens the\npattern to tolerate up to three intervening words and to recognise\nnumber words through \"twenty\", verified against both examples before\npublishing. Adds prose disclosing that the sweep also under-reports in\nthe opposite direction and that no regex closes that gap. Re-running\nthe widened sweep over README.md, docs/proposal, packages/*/README.md,\nand apps/*/README.md surfaced a small number of genuine stale-prone\ninventory counts, now reworded to drop the count while leaving\nlegitimate non-inventory prose (logical structure, anaphora, and\nclaims.md''s evidence-grounded C10) untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQvnhsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmKpeQD/fP0xEqEE3rpMgF+bRh+r\nFMkr9qBqXykJuaUdi/VXfOsA/jCoYuh+0LPpRVcrMQLM0pMiEBELVo1cbiWw48AW\nyzwL\n=syhh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDI2ZTU3NGU4YWQ4NTAwOTIyZmNkNWEwZjg3ZTIyNjNhNWQzODgwNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01","sha":"2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01"}],"sha":"26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/26e574e8ad8500922fcd5a0f87e2263a5d388078"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:43:13Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:43:13Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs: fix contradictory decision count and drop remaining inventory counts\n\nThe proposal''s architecture section said \"three decisions\" but listed\nfour ADR bullets, then separately said \"all four decisions\" a few\nlines later — a factual contradiction inside the deliverable itself.\nBoth sentences are rewritten to drop the count rather than correct\n\"three\" to \"four\", since a corrected count is still a count with no\nrunner.\n\nAlso drops the remaining inventory counts from the complete sweep:\ncontainer counts, list-introducing counts, and a closed-map count\nthat all go stale the moment something is added, while preserving the\nsentences'' load-bearing claims (e.g. the shell-contract event map\nstays described as \"closed\").","tree":{"sha":"1d2acb4c2244a8a54d55b55a32d66009e5f70694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/1d2acb4c2244a8a54d55b55a32d66009e5f70694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d2acb4c2244a8a54d55b55a32d66009e5f70694\nparent b9e730df79724e9391030015169f0c2bab945e85\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788093793 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788093793 +0700\n\ndocs: fix contradictory decision count and drop remaining inventory counts\n\nThe proposal''s architecture section said \"three decisions\" but listed\nfour ADR bullets, then separately said \"all four decisions\" a few\nlines later — a factual contradiction inside the deliverable itself.\nBoth sentences are rewritten to drop the count rather than correct\n\"three\" to \"four\", since a corrected count is still a count with no\nrunner.\n\nAlso drops the remaining inventory counts from the complete sweep:\ncontainer counts, list-introducing counts, and a closed-map count\nthat all go stale the moment something is added, while preserving the\nsentences'' load-bearing claims (e.g. the shell-contract event map\nstays described as \"closed\").\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQlYRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLIYgD7B2J0VaqNG4VOEMuLlG+j\nTRKwpwnJFgjJ0a1toO9jBhoBAJk+ZzQ+k1sQ6mlbWVMKGZcf5TA5oMluNsN5KwFw\ncJsA\n=NoB8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/2cb1f864a3bd4ec695bde4749ee11f8d1a725b01","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDJjYjFmODY0Y