iptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/70bd0811a1ea03518da13473ffcbe40040477fcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:35:15Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:35:15Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(docs): make C1''s evidence runnable, close the security-README gap, and drop spelled-out counts\n\nC1''s Evidence cell in docs/proposal/claims.md named only the smoke-test file,\nwhich passes identically whether or not the reference implementation was\never deleted. Replace it with the actual strip -> reinstall -> build -> e2e\nchain from the platform-only CI job, and warn readers in the preamble that\nthis command is destructive and belongs in a throwaway clone.\n\nsecurity/README.md never actually said what docs/proposal/README.md claimed\nit said about a maintainer owning the expiry date. Add that sentence to the\npolicy doc itself instead of softening the claim, without duplicating the\nallowlist''s specific date or advisory.\n\npackages/ui/README.md spelled out a component count in prose, which a wider\nsweep for spelled-out counts also caught in README.md and\napps/console/README.md; reworded all three to drop the counts.","tree":{"sha":"50baf5a958db6e70d114941d5e60a757216fddda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/50baf5a958db6e70d114941d5e60a757216fddda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/70bd0811a1ea03518da13473ffcbe40040477fcd","verification":{"payload":"tree 50baf5a958db6e70d114941d5e60a757216fddda\nparent 43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788093315 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788093315 +0700\n\nfix(docs): make C1''s evidence runnable, close the security-README gap, and drop spelled-out counts\n\nC1''s Evidence cell in docs/proposal/claims.md named only the smoke-test file,\nwhich passes identically whether or not the reference implementation was\never deleted. Replace it with the actual strip -> reinstall -> build -> e2e\nchain from the platform-only CI job, and warn readers in the preamble that\nthis command is destructive and belongs in a throwaway clone.\n\nsecurity/README.md never actually said what docs/proposal/README.md claimed\nit said about a maintainer owning the expiry date. Add that sentence to the\npolicy doc itself instead of softening the claim, without duplicating the\nallowlist''s specific date or advisory.\n\npackages/ui/README.md spelled out a component count in prose, which a wider\nsweep for spelled-out counts also caught in README.md and\napps/console/README.md; reworded all three to drop the counts.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQjgxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLO+wD/VYuBwZx64MsBFM13nSFb\nfngYmPvPD0VuIkmjXi5tDUEBANxXcPkSlxOWbf5PcQv0Xky0UnnSe4F1/MdrAxgD\nPcEK\n=4SwT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/70bd0811a1ea03518da13473ffcbe40040477fcd","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDcwYmQwODExYTFlYTAzNTE4ZGExMzQ3M2ZmY2JlNDAwNDA0NzdmY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4","sha":"43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4"}],"sha":"70bd0811a1ea03518da13473ffcbe40040477fcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/70bd0811a1ea03518da13473ffcbe40040477fcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:23:39Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:23:39Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(csp): stop emitting frame-ancestors in the meta-delivered policy\n\nframe-ancestors is ignored by browsers when a CSP is delivered via\n<meta>, per the spec, and Chrome logs a console error about it on\nevery load. Since Task 6 wired CSP generation into the shell''s build,\nthat error fires on every build, including the platform-only job''s\nmocked build, and fails the platform-only smoke test''s zero-console-\nerror assertion (a live red CI gate, not hypothetical).\n\nscripts/csp.mjs now builds two policy strings: buildCspPolicy (the\nheader form, byte-identical to before) and buildCspPolicyForMeta,\nwhich omits frame-ancestors, report-uri, and report-to (the\nMETA_IGNORED_DIRECTIVES set — directives a meta tag can never\nenforce). generate-csp.mjs injects the meta form into index.html and\nwrites the header form to csp-headers.txt, so a real server fronting\nthe shell still gets the full policy, frame-ancestors included.\n\nThis is not a security weakening: the directive was never enforced in\nmeta form, so removing it from the meta tag changes nothing a browser\nwas doing. Clickjacking protection depends on an operator serving\ncsp-headers.txt''s content as a real header, as ADR 0008 already states.\n\nRestores claim C1 in docs/proposal/claims.md, deleted by Task 14 when\nits evidence (this same smoke test) failed; the evidence now passes.","tree":{"sha":"f0eec480aac8325a1778782b4ce26fdc9d733af6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/f0eec480aac8325a1778782b4ce26fdc9d733af6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4","verification":{"payload":"tree f0eec480aac8325a1778782b4ce26fdc9d733af6\nparent 371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788092619 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788092619 +0700\n\nfix(csp): stop emitting frame-ancestors in the meta-delivered policy\n\nframe-ancestors is ignored by browsers when a CSP is delivered via\n<meta>, per the spec, and Chrome logs a console error about it on\nevery load. Since Task 6 wired CSP generation into the shell''s build,\nthat error fires on every build, including the platform-only job''s\nmocked build, and fails the platform-only smoke test''s zero-console-\nerror assertion (a live red CI gate, not hypothetical).\n\nscripts/csp.mjs now builds two policy strings: buildCspPolicy (the\nheader form, byte-identical to before) and buildCspPolicyForMeta,\nwhich omits frame-ancestors, report-uri, and report-to (the\nMETA_IGNORED_DIRECTIVES set — directives a meta tag can never\nenforce). generate-csp.mjs injects the meta form into index.html and\nwrites the header form to csp-headers.txt, so a real server fronting\nthe shell still gets the full policy, frame-ancestors included.\n\nThis is not a security weakening: the directive was never enforced in\nmeta form, so removing it from the meta tag changes nothing a browser\nwas doing. Clickjacking protection depends on an operator serving\ncsp-headers.txt''s content as a real header, as ADR 0008 already states.\n\nRestores claim C1 in docs/proposal/claims.md, deleted by Task 14 when\nits evidence (this same smoke test) failed; the evidence now passes.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQgyxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLqPgEAnv2v13LHA92bCQLp6GIL\nQkme8sM1gv1xlmn8iq4EtjUBAILB9qBV2D1yL8F5Cj9AmBpOxwDdLyo7Ai2q0ItL\n60gB\n=+i9f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDQzODM4ZmE5OTBkZDRjMzdiMzg1YjliMjY2NzMzOTY4Mjc0YWYyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a","sha":"371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a"}],"sha":"43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/43838fa990dd4c37b385b9b266733968274af2f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:08:48Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:08:48Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs: write the platform proposal and rewrite the README as a template\n\nFills in all eight sections of docs/proposal/README.md with the platform''s\nvalue proposition, architecture rationale (linked to ADRs 0001-0009), the\nbatteries-included/not boundary, what each of the five CI gates does and does\nnot prove (including every carried known issue by file/line), the adoption\nprocedure, and the ongoing costs.\n\ndocs/proposal/claims.md gains a Verified column. Claim C1 (platform boots\nwith zero console errors after the reference implementation is deleted) is\ndeleted rather than softened: apps/shell/e2e-platform-only/platform-only.smoke.spec.ts:70\nfails deterministically on a real Chrome console warning that meta-tag CSP\ndelivery cannot avoid (documented in ADR 0008), a defect the smoke test''s\nstrict assertion was never reconciled with. Its cause and the deleted claim''s\nprior text are recorded in claims.md itself.\n\nThe root README is rewritten as a template landing page: what the repo is\nfor, a batteries-included/not table, a platform/reference role table naming\nthe deletion command, and a link to the proposal. All hardcoded counts are\nremoved, including the \"486 tests\" line, in favor of the commands that print\nthe current numbers. All 6 CI jobs are now listed (lighthouse and\nplatform-only were missing). The single-v-html design-principle claim is\nscoped to the reference-owned file it actually describes.\n\nEvery workspace member''s README gets a one-line Role declaration: platform\ncore, or reference implementation with a link to the removal procedure.\n\nAlso adds ADR 0003 (reference-owned) to sentra.referenceDocs in package.json,\nso scripts/strip-reference.mjs removes it along with the reference\nimplementation it documents.","tree":{"sha":"e7784db3a7314fb8afec0616a2b9701c58c391a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/e7784db3a7314fb8afec0616a2b9701c58c391a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/371173af30c842015ec4c83e9e636d4c1fc73e0a","verification":{"payload":"tree e7784db3a7314fb8afec0616a2b9701c58c391a0\nparent 7a75be67ad0f8c5b98dc36ebc3eeb16c15cd3c2d\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788091728 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788091728 +0700\n\ndocs: write the platform proposal and rewrite the README as a template\n\nFills in all eight sections of docs/proposal/README.md with the platform''s\nvalue proposition, architecture rationale (linked to ADRs 0001-0009), the\nbatteries-included/not boundary, what each of the five CI gates does and does\nnot prove (including every carried known issue by file/line), the adoption\nprocedure, and the ongoing costs.\n\ndocs/proposal/claims.md gains a Verified column. Claim C1 (platform boots\nwith zero console errors after the reference implementation is deleted) is\ndeleted rather than softened: apps/shell/e2e-platform-only/platform-only.smoke.spec.ts:70\nfails deterministically on a real Chrome console warning that meta-tag CSP\ndelivery cannot avoid (documented in ADR 0008), a defect the smoke test''s\nstrict assertion was never reconciled with. Its cause and the deleted claim''s\nprior text are recorded in claims.md itself.\n\nThe root README is rewritten as a template landing page: what the repo is\nfor, a batteries-included/not table, a platform/reference role table naming\nthe deletion command, and a link to the proposal. All hardcoded counts are\nremoved, including the \"486 tests\" line, in favor of the commands that print\nthe current numbers. All 6 CI jobs are now listed (lighthouse and\nplatform-only were missing). The single-v-html design-principle claim is\nscoped to the reference-owned file it actually describes.\n\nEvery workspace member''s README gets a one-line Role declaration: platform\ncore, or reference implementation with a link to the removal procedure.\n\nAlso adds ADR 0003 (reference-owned) to sentra.referenceDocs in package.json,\nso scripts/strip-reference.mjs removes it along with the reference\nimplementation it documents.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQdUBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLeRAEA1YBNqfZ0MUE8FlakIdoB\nKpQ05vN5xUlAM7sORXzNm74A/1L9bkUt14qx7gD8A79XZgyS+6d50GVub7TxQLox\nYCEN\n=XNmb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"ht