omment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T11:07:38Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"perf(ci): build once per E2E job instead of twice","tree":{"sha":"368700ba5250dacc41c04622c27af8a20001f8db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/368700ba5250dacc41c04622c27af8a20001f8db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/824aa9b0ecfecda2ac598afcd4cd6b8ff34e11de","verification":{"payload":"tree 368700ba5250dacc41c04622c27af8a20001f8db\nparent 0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788088058 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788088058 +0700\n\nperf(ci): build once per E2E job instead of twice\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQO+hsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmLXjgEAviQPe2eeFbyEg7bMVjzR\noMEBr4CtapaLr6AdPv1nEmoBANs2aMfjI2CrA6hd17w3a2giW9GokuSA3QRBtKj6\nnD0K\n=DaN8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/824aa9b0ecfecda2ac598afcd4cd6b8ff34e11de","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDgyNGFhOWIwZWNmZWNkYTJhYzU5OGFmY2Q0Y2Q2YjhmZjM0ZTExZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e","sha":"0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e"}],"sha":"824aa9b0ecfecda2ac598afcd4cd6b8ff34e11de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/824aa9b0ecfecda2ac598afcd4cd6b8ff34e11de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T11:01:08Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T11:01:08Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix(turbo): declare @sentra/sdk-commerce''s real build output\n\nEvery `pnpm build` printed:\n\n  WARNING  no output files found for task @sentra/sdk-commerce#build.\n  Please check your `outputs` key in `turbo.json`\n\nThe root `build` task declares `outputs: [\"dist/**\"]`, but sdk-commerce''s\nbuild is `graphql-codegen`, which writes into `src/generated/`. Turbo was\ntherefore caching an empty artifact set for that task and saying so on\nevery run. A warning that fires on every build is a warning nobody reads,\nwhich is how the real one gets missed.\n\nAdds a task-specific `@sentra/sdk-commerce#build` entry declaring\n`src/generated/**`. Task-specific config replaces the base entry rather\nthan merging, so `dependsOn: [\"^build\"]` is restated; `env:\n[\"VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS\"]` is deliberately not, because codegen reads a\nvendored schema and a static document set and cannot vary with the mock\nflag.\n\nVerified: warning gone, `pnpm build` green, an unchanged rerun reports 6\ncached of 6, and the working tree is clean after a forced rebuild — so the\ncommitted contents of `src/generated/` currently match what codegen\nproduces.\n\nNot verified, and worth stating plainly: that a cache *hit* restores those\nfiles. The first attempt at that check deleted `src/generated/` and\nobserved the files return, but the turbo log shows\n`@sentra/sdk-commerce:build: cache miss, executing` — deleting files inside\nthe package changes its own input hash, so codegen simply re-ran and the\ncheck proved nothing. Since these outputs live inside the package''s input\nset, no scenario leaves inputs unchanged while outputs are missing, and the\nrestore path is not reachable to test from here. The declaration''s value is\nthat the cache entry now holds the real artifacts instead of nothing.\n\nThe generated files are committed (three tracked files under\n`src/generated/`), so nothing depends on cache restore for correctness.","tree":{"sha":"adba776cbe78affd26840ad2aa4f6d2501d91d44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/adba776cbe78affd26840ad2aa4f6d2501d91d44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e","verification":{"payload":"tree adba776cbe78affd26840ad2aa4f6d2501d91d44\nparent 45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788087668 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788087668 +0700\n\nfix(turbo): declare @sentra/sdk-commerce''s real build output\n\nEvery `pnpm build` printed:\n\n  WARNING  no output files found for task @sentra/sdk-commerce#build.\n  Please check your `outputs` key in `turbo.json`\n\nThe root `build` task declares `outputs: [\"dist/**\"]`, but sdk-commerce''s\nbuild is `graphql-codegen`, which writes into `src/generated/`. Turbo was\ntherefore caching an empty artifact set for that task and saying so on\nevery run. A warning that fires on every build is a warning nobody reads,\nwhich is how the real one gets missed.\n\nAdds a task-specific `@sentra/sdk-commerce#build` entry declaring\n`src/generated/**`. Task-specific config replaces the base entry rather\nthan merging, so `dependsOn: [\"^build\"]` is restated; `env:\n[\"VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS\"]` is deliberately not, because codegen reads a\nvendored schema and a static document set and cannot vary with the mock\nflag.\n\nVerified: warning gone, `pnpm build` green, an unchanged rerun reports 6\ncached of 6, and the working tree is clean after a forced rebuild — so the\ncommitted contents of `src/generated/` currently match what codegen\nproduces.\n\nNot verified, and worth stating plainly: that a cache *hit* restores those\nfiles. The first attempt at that check deleted `src/generated/` and\nobserved the files return, but the turbo log shows\n`@sentra/sdk-commerce:build: cache miss, executing` — deleting files inside\nthe package changes its own input hash, so codegen simply re-ran and the\ncheck proved nothing. Since these outputs live inside the package''s input\nset, no scenario leaves inputs unchanged while outputs are missing, and the\nrestore path is not reachable to test from here. The declaration''s value is\nthat the cache entry now holds the real artifacts instead of nothing.\n\nThe generated files are committed (three tracked files under\n`src/generated/`), so nothing depends on cache restore for correctness.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQNdBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmItQQD/bPcMVwbbnVVyUawG8BXu\nXAqjTR2JJK2++CN3ZKeZeAQA/ikeKGkhzm21/3uYquthYreJROq3gUGxtNMdXfum\nM9gH\n=Ama0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e","node_id":"C_kwDOUF6bmdoAKDBkNmE1MTY0YTdjY2M2ZWIxMjVlNTNkY2Y3ZWEyZWFkZmQ0MTA5OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94","sha":"45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94"}],"sha":"0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/0d6a5164a7ccc6eb125e53dcf7ea2eadfd41098e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:57:16Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:57:16Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"fix: make @sentra/ui''s build fail on broken types, and clear the audit gate\n\nTwo findings from investigating a \"pre-existing warning\" flagged during\nTask 10. Both are in one commit because they share a lockfile that cannot\nbe split without leaving an intermediate commit whose package.json and\npnpm-lock.yaml disagree.\n\n1. @sentra/ui built green while emitting eleven errors.\n\n`vite build` ran vite-plugin-dts, which type-checks with plain tsc and so\ncannot resolve `*.vue` imports. It reported eleven TS2307 errors, emitted\ndeclarations for only the five non-SFC modules out of eighteen, and let\nthe build exit 0 anyway. The gate said \"built\" whether or not the package\nhad usable types — the same shape of defect this milestone has been\nremoving everywhere else: an assertion that holds regardless of whether\nthe asserted thing is true.\n\nReplaced the plugin with a direct `vue-tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` step in\nthe build script. vue-tsc understands single-file components, emits all\neighteen declarations, and propagates a non-zero exit. Verified by\nmutation: a type-only error that Vite strips without complaint (esbuild\ndoes not type-check) now takes the build to exit 2 after Vite itself\nsucceeds — so the failure comes from the checker, not from the bundler.\n`tsconfig.build.json` gains explicit rootDir/outDir, which the plugin had\nbeen supplying and which vue-tsc reports as TS5011 without.\n\nvite-plugin-dts is dropped from devDependencies; packages/config/README.md\ndescribed it as this repository''s declaration emitter and no longer does.\n\n2. verify:audit was already red on this branch.\n\nIndependently reproduced against the pre-change lockfile, so this predates\nthe change above. Both blocking advisories arrive through @lhci/cli, added\nfor the Lighthouse budgets in Task 8. Named risk area: supply chain.\n\n  GHSA-ph9p-34f9-6g65 (tmp, high) — patched in >=0.2.6. Reached twice, both\n  times transitively, so a pnpm override is the only lever. Pinned to\n  ^0.2.6; this also clears GHSA-52f5-9888-hmc6 (tmp, low). tmp now resolves\n  to a single 0.2.7 across both paths.\n\n  GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv (extract-zip, high) — the advisory records\n  patched_versions `<0.0.0` against a vulnerable range of `<=2.0.1`, and\n  2.0.1 is the latest published version. There is nothing to upgrade to,\n  so it is accepted in security/audit-allowlist.json with a reason and a\n  2026-11-28 deadline, per the gate''s own escape hatch.\n\nGHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq (uuid, moderate) remains reported and unfixed: it is\nbelow the gate''s high/critical threshold, and overriding uuid repo-wide\nwould move consumers pinned across two majors for a non-blocking finding.\n\nThe allowlist''s `$schema` pointed at ./allowlist.schema.md, which does not\nexist in this repository; it now points at the README that documents the\nentry format.\n\nVerified green after the change: format:check, lint, verify:roles,\ntypecheck, build, test (624), verify:sourcemaps, verify:bundle-size,\nverify:csp, verify:audit, verify:lighthouse, verify:lighthouse:reference.\nThe two Lighthouse gates matter here specifically because they exercise\n@lhci/cli against the overridden tmp.","tree":{"sha":"f8bbdc360161e9195ec0fe80f85fe58c81989233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/f8bbdc360161e9195ec0fe80f85fe58c81989233"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94","verification":{"payload":"tree f8bbdc360161e9195ec0fe80f85fe58c81989233\nparent a5580dc818c17c83ef289eda1b367483871d63f6\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788087436 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788087436 +0700\n\nfix: make @sentra/ui''s build fail on broken types, and clear the audit gate\n\nTwo findings from investigating a \"pre-existing warning\" flagged during\nTask 10. Both are in one commit because they share a lockfile that cannot\nbe split without leaving an intermediate commit whose package.json and\npnpm-lock.yaml disagree.\n\n1. @sentra/ui built green while emitting eleven errors.\n\n`vite build` ran vite-plugin-dts, which type-checks with plain tsc and so\ncannot resolve `*.vue` imports. It reported eleven TS2307 errors, emitted\ndeclarations for only the five non-SFC modules out of eighteen, and let\nthe build exit 0 anyway. The gate said \"built\" whether or not the package\nhad usable types — the same shape of defect this milestone has been\nremoving everywhere else: an assertion that holds regardless of whether\nthe asserted thing is true.\n\nReplaced the plugin with a direct `vue-tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` step in\nthe build script. vue-tsc understands single-file components, emits all\neighteen declarations, and propagates a non-zero exit. Verified by\nmutation: a type-only error that Vite strips without complaint (esbuild\ndoes not type-check) now takes the build to exit 2 after Vite itself\nsucceeds — so the failure comes from the checker, not from the bundler.\n`tsconfig.build.json` gains explicit rootDir/outDir, which the plugin had\nbeen supplying and which vue-tsc reports as TS5011 without.\n\nvite-plugin-dts is dropped from devDependencies; packages/config/README.md\ndescribed it as this repository''s declaration emitter and no longer does.\n\n2. verify:audit was already red on this branch.\n\nIndependently reproduced against the pre-change lockfile, so this predates\nthe change above. Both blocking advisories arrive through @lhci/cli, added\nfor the Lighthouse budgets in Task 8. Named risk area: supply chain.\n\n  GHSA-ph9p-34f9-6g65 (tmp, high) — patched in >=0.2.6. Reached twice, both\n  times transitively, so a pnpm override is the only lever. Pinned to\n  ^0.2.6; this also clears GHSA-52f5-9888-hmc6 (tmp, low). tmp now resolves\n  to a single 0.2.7 across both paths.\n\n  GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv (extract-zip, high) — the advisory records\n  patched_versions `<0.0.0` against a vulnerable range of `<=2.0.1`, and\n  2.0.1 is the latest published version. There is nothing to upgrade to,\n  so it is accepted in security/audit-allowlist.json with a reason and a\n  2026-11-28 deadline, per the gate''s own escape hatch.\n\nGHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq (uuid, moderate) remains reported and unfixed: it is\nbelow the gate''s high/critical threshold, and overriding uuid repo-wide\nwould move consumers pinned across two majors for a non-blocking finding.\n\nThe allowlist''s `$schema` pointed at ./allowlist.schema.md, which does not\nexist in this repository; it now points at the README that documents the\nentry format.\n\nVerified green after the change: format:check, lint, verify:roles,\ntypecheck, build, test (624), verify:sourcemaps, verify:bundle-size,\nverify:csp, verify:audit, verify:lighthouse, verify:lighthouse:reference.\nThe two Lighthouse gates matter here specifically because they exercise\n@lhci/cli against the overridden tmp.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapQMjRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmKeJAEA717K3Po4uIs2AniI8kYt\n0lUTLTmF9nT6IrfrQcOfTXwBAIe0dIRzJxra0qDhM9LL6Qn7jAMzzsMeW3Dwcior\nzc0N\n=Cl3D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda/sentra/commit/45736fdb67bee3176747275a90969dc6dc2a2e94","node