owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barayuda","id":520463,"login":"barayuda","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDQ2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/74d43ec950a4525184658a36a5c05f0ac5513389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:27:46Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:27:46Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"docs(gates): document that Lighthouse budgets cannot assert a resource floor\n\n@lhci/cli 0.15.1''s assertion vocabulary is exactly {minScore, maxLength,\nmaxNumericValue} -- minNumericValue does not exist, verified against\nnode_modules/@lhci/utils/src/assertions.js. Every resource-summary\nassertion in both configs is maxNumericValue, an upper bound only, so a\nbuild that emits nothing passes all of them (0 <= any budget), and\ncategories:accessibility at minScore 1 does not catch it either: a\nsyntactically valid, fully empty page scores a perfect 1.0.\n\nThe resource floor is enforced upstream by scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs\ninstead, whose classify()/evaluate() already fail loudly on a missing or\nempty dist/ -- verified by emptying apps/shell/dist and re-running\nverify:bundle-size. Documented in both $comments so a future reader does\nnot assume five maxNumericValue lines cover a case they do not.","tree":{"sha":"9756654ed78b2597745fafbc5197ae961a575ec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/9756654ed78b2597745fafbc5197ae961a575ec8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/74d43ec950a4525184658a36a5c05f0ac5513389","verification":{"payload":"tree 9756654ed78b2597745fafbc5197ae961a575ec8\nparent 4c62d686b4f8ddbae0ac4bff6558f4316fc59a1f\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788078466 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788078466 +0700\n\ndocs(gates): document that Lighthouse budgets cannot assert a resource floor\n\n@lhci/cli 0.15.1''s assertion vocabulary is exactly {minScore, maxLength,\nmaxNumericValue} -- minNumericValue does not exist, verified against\nnode_modules/@lhci/utils/src/assertions.js. Every resource-summary\nassertion in both configs is maxNumericValue, an upper bound only, so a\nbuild that emits nothing passes all of them (0 <= any budget), and\ncategories:accessibility at minScore 1 does not catch it either: a\nsyntactically valid, fully empty page scores a perfect 1.0.\n\nThe resource floor is enforced upstream by scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs\ninstead, whose classify()/evaluate() already fail loudly on a missing or\nempty dist/ -- verified by emptying apps/shell/dist and re-running\nverify:bundle-size. Documented in both $comments so a future reader does\nnot assume five maxNumericValue lines cover a case they do not.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapPpghsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmKNpwD8CdfaaDxP4IGgmGsRarVG\naWl8teLbgGCPEF7rgdbRLBIA/1XVkp9UXyjODQUNimpzy7j6Ej0kqPDwASdBEkWt\n9NkA\n=VOkZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/520463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b