s","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barayuda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/commits/0cf1b96731a932f40c3cf124473772b3ebc49a0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:11:40Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:11:40Z","email":"520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Bara Yuda"},"message":"chore: merge M4 — module federation shell, ops console, dual-mode storefront\n\nAdds runtime Module Federation across three containers.\n\n- packages/result — the Result convention extracted for reuse by two SDKs\n- packages/shell-contract — RemoteModule contract, typed ShellEventMap bus,\n  shell-owned session\n- packages/sdk-ops — ops REST SDK, four-arm OpsError union, MSW mocks\n- apps/shell — federation host: fetches and validates public/remotes.json,\n  registerRemotes({ force: true }) then loadRemote(), grafts remote routes,\n  enforces role guards, degrades to RemoteUnavailable on failure\n- apps/console — new ops remote (server-sorted orders, optimistic flags)\n- apps/storefront — converted to a dual-mode remote, standalone still works\n\nRemotes are registered at runtime from a manifest rather than bound at build\ntime, so repointing one is a JSON edit on the host''s static assets. The\nmanifest is a supply-chain boundary and allow-lists http:/https: only.\n\nADRs 0004 (runtime remote registry), 0005 (shared singletons and the\nstring-injection-key rule), 0006 (cross-remote communication).\n\n23 commits, 486 tests, all gates green.","tree":{"sha":"55ff95a6d782cf1139a2035467c5c09584ec7fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/trees/55ff95a6d782cf1139a2035467c5c09584ec7fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/barayuda/sentra/git/commits/0cf1b96731a932f40c3cf124473772b3ebc49a0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 55ff95a6d782cf1139a2035467c5c09584ec7fd5\nparent 70041ab84da3c06cf57853a760d7453573cca981\nparent 665cb39b2576f3328dd732730032054e0e55fada\nauthor Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788045100 +0700\ncommitter Bara Yuda <520463+barayuda@users.noreply.github.com> 1788045100 +0700\n\nchore: merge M4 — module federation shell, ops console, dual-mode storefront\n\nAdds runtime Module Federation across three containers.\n\n- packages/result — the Result convention extracted for reuse by two SDKs\n- packages/shell-contract — RemoteModule contract, typed ShellEventMap bus,\n  shell-owned session\n- packages/sdk-ops — ops REST SDK, four-arm OpsError union, MSW mocks\n- apps/shell — federation host: fetches and validates public/remotes.json,\n  registerRemotes({ force: true }) then loadRemote(), grafts remote routes,\n  enforces role guards, degrades to RemoteUnavailable on failure\n- apps/console — new ops remote (server-sorted orders, optimistic flags)\n- apps/storefront — converted to a dual-mode remote, standalone still works\n\nRemotes are registered at runtime from a manifest rather than bound at build\ntime, so repointing one is a JSON edit on the host''s static assets. The\nmanifest is a supply-chain boundary and allow-lists http:/https: only.\n\nADRs 0004 (runtime remote registry), 0005 (shared singletons and the\nstring-injection-key rule), 0006 (cross-remote communication).\n\n23 commits, 486 tests, all gates green.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQT5aaSSLDPHgHvQqUbi3Urahf46YgUCapNnLBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQ4t1K2oX+OmJTLgEAt59hvCA/QBDmTC6eb8hL\nse9WUBdRI/aa24e6VfwEsBYA/0GzkqqIgeIOQJDAq3DJW70ZqW5+WVBH1oVHqN9P\npSIN\n=WCNM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T14:46:15Z"}},"committer":{"ava