/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/8081c0f338b71c678a764e3ffe9629cef8a377d3","node_id":"C_kwDOUGYItNoAKDgwODFjMGYzMzhiNzFjNjc4YTc2NGUzZmZlOTYyOWNlZjhhMzc3ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","sha":"7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701","sha":"fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701"}],"sha":"8081c0f338b71c678a764e3ffe9629cef8a377d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/8081c0f338b71c678a764e3ffe9629cef8a377d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:35:55Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:35:55Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"message":"Make the lab readable, winnable and fun\n\nWalked the lab end to end as a learner first, then fixed what that turned\nup. Four themes.\n\nInstructions: task first, concept second. Every step doc used to spend\n~40 lines on Concept before saying what to type; each now opens with\n\"Do this\" (file, change, verify command) and puts the concept below the\nfold, with a ticket line and a time estimate. Repeated explanations are\ndeduplicated to one canonical home apiece — the tsconfig path-mapping\ntrap was told seven times, the dev-server restart rule nine. Adds\nguide/CHEATSHEET.md: all six changes on one screen.\n\nAchievement: a scoreboard you can actually win. s5 (strictVersion) and\ns6 (DESIGN.md) leave no runtime trace, so the dashboard reported them\n\"unknown\" forever and 25 of the advertised 100 points were unreachable.\nA Jest reporter now writes .lab/status.json, served at /lab-status.json\nfrom a dev-server middleware — not apps/shell/public/, which would trip\nthe asset watcher on every test run. Each step shows two verdicts side\nby side, live and npm test, so the two independent checks agreeing is\nvisible rather than asserted. A sessionStorage high-water mark stops the\nscore regressing from 4/6 to 3/6 on navigation. Stale results no longer\ngrant a pass, and a genuine live-vs-test contradiction is surfaced with\nits likely cause instead of being silently resolved.\n\nInteractive. The blast-radius experiment runs for real in two stages:\nthe outage you can watch, then the reload that takes the dashboard down\nwith it. A flag survives the blackout so the panel reopens with the\ndebrief. serveApps finally has the `hide` option TOUR.md and guide/06\nhad been documenting but which never existed, behind npm run\nblast-radius — a real 404 rather than the SPA fallback''s misleading\n200 text/html. Adds a what-just-changed ticker built from the snapshot\ndiff the probe was already computing and discarding.\n\nUI. /lab declared its own --lab-* tokens and then ignored the type\nscale — hardcoded 13/14/20px, no .card anywhere — which is exactly the\ndebug-overlay look its own comment said it wanted to avoid. Rebuilt on\nthe storefront''s design system: progress ring, step board with real\nverdict hierarchy, six named achievement badges, a completion card with\na paste-ready summary, and a day-one first-run state in place of a wall\nof red. Checked in dark mode and at 375px.\n\nAlso fixes an unrelated bug found while testing: start:remote:watch hung\non roughly every other restart because nodemon''s default SIGTERM left\nthe Nx daemon mid-write, and the next nx serve blocked forever on\n\"Calculating the project graph\". --signal SIGINT fixes it. It struck\nprecisely when a learner edits a federation config, which is when they\nare waiting on feedback.\n\nThe four lab-solution files are untouched: npm test still reports the\ndocumented 11 of 18 failing from a clean checkout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95b18d72be60d865ab8725fe109946bd02cb5332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/trees/95b18d72be60d865ab8725fe109946bd02cb5332"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/commits/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701","node_id":"C_kwDOUGYItNoAKGZiYzlhZjlhMDZkNWNlMzA1YmMyMGEzYjdmYmE4NjU5MDViZWE3MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","sha":"7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15"}],"sha":"fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/fbc9af9a06d5ce305bc20a3b7fba865905bea701"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:23:12Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:23:12Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"message":"Make it a real storefront, not a scaffold\n\nThe two applications were bare Angular scaffolds: an unstyled header, a four-line\nproduct list, one hardcoded card. That is fine for testing federation config and\nuseless for feeling why federation is hard — which only shows up when two teams\nhave to cooperate on a page a user would actually accept.\n\nSo it is now Acme Storefront. styles/theme.css is a small design system (warm\npalette, rounded geometry, light and dark) imported by BOTH applications as plain\nCSS rather than a federated library; the file explains why, and what that costs.\n\n  shell     brand, nav, sign-in, a working basket with a popover, a 404, a footer\n            that credits which application rendered what\n  products  a ten-item catalogue with departments, filters, sort, ratings, stock\n            and sale pricing, over per-SKU generated SVG artwork (no binary assets)\n\nTwo additions carry real teaching weight:\n\n- The basket moved into libs/shared-auth. The REMOTE owns the Add-to-basket\n  buttons; the SHELL owns the header counter. Nothing imports anything across that\n  line, so the only reason a click on one moves the other is that both resolved to\n  one shared store. Get step 3 wrong and the button works, the counter never moves,\n  and nothing reports an error. Verified both ways: two store ids and a dead\n  counter before, one id and a live counter after. Deliberately NOT persisted —\n  two copies hydrating from one sessionStorage key would launder exactly this bug.\n- The home page''s featured slot now distinguishes `federated` from `bundled`. It\n  used to say \"from the products remote\" whenever the import resolved, which on a\n  fresh clone is a lie: the tsconfig path mapping satisfies it and webpack compiles\n  the card into the host. It now asks the network instead and says so in as many\n  words when no remoteEntry.mjs was fetched. That turns the trap into the most\n  useful thing on the page.\n\nAlso: /products used to render blank with a router error before step 2, which reads\nas a broken repo. It gets a real 404 that names the step. Its wildcard route lives\nin app.config.ts, not app.routes.ts — a `**` at the bottom of the file you edit in\nstep 2 would silently swallow the route you add after it.\n\nVerified end to end at both ends of the lab: on the stub, 11 of 18 checks fail as\nbefore and the UI reports every step honestly; solved, 17 of 18 pass, the dashboard\nreads 75/100 required-track-complete, and the remote''s buttons drive the shell''s\nbasket. Angular unit tests grew to 16.\n\nprettier is pinned at 2.x, which predates Angular''s `@if`/`@for` blocks and mangles\nevery template it formats, so component files are now in .prettierignore and\nhand-formatted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6f2566901dd0dd85903c3768464b5a4493cdaae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/trees/e6f2566901dd0dd85903c3768464b5a4493cdaae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/commits/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","node_id":"C_kwDOUGYItNoAKDc3NzhjNTJlNjUzZmZiY2ViOTA3OGJlOWIxMTY2MzA4YzU3YmNhMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628","sha":"5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628"}],"sha":"7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/7778c52e653ffbceb9078be9b1166308c57bca15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T19:18:27Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T19:18:27Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"message":"Fix the doctor''s port check, and drop the unused third port\n\nThe port check bound the port to see if that failed, which reported 4271 and 4272\nfree while the dev servers were running: they listen on 127.0.0.1, an unqualified\nbind lands on ::, and macOS lets the two coexist. A check that says \"free\" moments\nbefore the candidate gets EADDRINUSE is worse than no check, so it now probes by\nconnecting, on both stacks.\n\n4273 was only ever used by Nx''s static-remotes mode, which this lab no longer goes\nnear now that the shell serves through the plain dev-server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7467ad909b828f7c3d642796e495f29cc37167f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/trees/7467ad909b828f7c3d642796e495f29cc37167f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/commits/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628","node_id":"C_kwDOUGYItNoAKDVmOWZmMzRlN2I5ZDI5MGI5MGFmZWNmYjBiNDc2NDUzYjYwMTE2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f","sha":"cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f"}],"sha":"5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/5f9ff34e7b9d290b90afecfb0b476453b6011628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T19:16:34Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T19:16:34Z","email":"yusheng.zhang@antra.com","name":"JR"},"message":"Microfrontend Module Federation lab, runnable locally\n\nA six-step guided lab: wire an Nx host and remote together with webpack Module\nFederation, get the share scope and version policy right, then argue the design.\n\nExported from the Antra-LMS in-browser lab and reworked for a candidate''s own\nmachine, which changed three things:\n\n- The step guidance is written out in guide/, all six steps fully open (concept,\n  task, how to check, hints, solution). The LMS rendered this from a database and\n  gated later steps; neither makes sense in a git repo you clone.\n- The graded harness is replaced by unit tests in tests/. The old one built both\n  apps and drove headless Chromium (~2 min, and a Chrome prerequisite); these read\n  the config files directly and run in seconds. Failures are written to teach.\n- libs/lab-dashboard is new: a live view at /lab of what the two applications are\n  actually doing — federation diagram, the runtime share scope, SessionStore\n  instance count, step checklist, and a blast-radius exercise. It replaces the\n  platform''s step rail and supplies the runtime proof unit tests cannot.\n\nNotes on two things that bit during the port, both documented in SETUP.md:\n\n- A rendered Products page is not evidence of federation. tsconfig.base.json maps\n  the federated specifiers at the remote''s real sources, so the import resolves\n  with no remote declared. The dashboard''s step 2 probe therefore looks for an\n  actual remoteEntry.mjs request, and was verified against that failure mode.\n- Step 5 is deliberately never reported done by the dashboard: Nx already defaults\n  @angular/core to singleton + strictVersion, so the runtime cannot distinguish a\n  declared policy from a defaulted one. npm test owns that step.\n\napps/shell''s serve target moved from module-federation-dev-server to the plain\ndev-server — the former''s runtime-library-control plugin calls a webpack parser API\nthat webpack 5.109 removed — and gained historyApiFallback so /lab and /products\nsurvive a reload. The pinned lockfile is preserved byte-for-byte apart from its\nroot identity; @rspack/core stays on 1.3.15, which is load-bearing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6916b3b57d146e09a118791e5ba4b6410b668755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/trees/6916b3b57d146e09a118791e5ba4b6410b668755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/git/commits/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90920899?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra","id":90920899,"login":"JRAntra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTIwODk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JRAntra","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commit/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f","node_id":"C_kwDOUGYItNoAKGNjMThiZGQ0NDEyOWQ0NGE4OTk3YjA2ZTAyOWMyMTFjY2U2MTQ4OWY","parents":[],"sha":"cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits/cc18bdd44129d44a8997b06e029c211cce61489f"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/JRAntra/micro-frontend-practice/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=8081c0f338b71c678a764e3ffe9629cef8a377d3&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A44%3A00.248Z"}');
